\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 9-16 BTC, ETH, SOL, TON, DOT, WIF, XRP\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,743 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Markets Await FOMC And Powell Speech}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Poised For Huge Rally}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC Comes In For Criticism}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toncoin (TON) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple (XRP) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) saw considerable fluctuations over the weekend. It briefly pushed above $60,000 as market sentiment showed signs of shifting, resulting in a temporary jump of 6%.\par \par \uc2 BTC is currently down almost 3%, slipping below $60,000 during early trading. Meanwhile, Ethereum (ETH) fell below $2,300 as trading began, dropping as low as $2,259 and almost 6% over the past 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 Other major cryptocurrencies, including Carnado (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Dogecoin (DOGE), Toncoin (TON), Polkadot (DOT), Uniswap (UNI), Solana (SOL), and FET have also opened the week in the red, registering substantial drops over the past 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Markets Await FOMC And Powell Speech\par \par \uc2 The crypto market is set to enter yet another crucial week as speculation mounts about a 50 bps rate cut by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , which could significantly impact the broader financial markets. Additionally, Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  is set to speak after the FOMC meeting in a speech expected to provide insight into the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s stance on policy rate plans. With the recent US CPI and PPI inflation numbers, markets are betting on a 0.5% Fed rate cut during the upcoming meeting.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the broader financial markets have registered an uptick, as US markets notched their best trading week since last September. BTC\u8217\'20\'19s brief push above $60,000 also hinted at an increasing risk-bet appetite of market participants. The \uc2 CME\uc2  FedWatch tool has allotted a 50% probability for a 50 bps rate cut. At the same time, the odds for a smaller rate cut of 0.25% are also the same.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  is also set to speak following the FOMC meeting on September 18, an event the crypto market will keep a keen eye on. The Fed Chair is expected to take a dovish stance. Still, any other move could significantly hamper broader market sentiment, especially after BTC and other major altcoins registered a recovery last week in anticipation of a larger interest rate cut.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Poised For Huge Rally\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Michael van de Poppe anticipates that the crypto and commodities markets are poised for a massive rally fueled by an upcoming surge in global liquidity, driven by debt refinancing, which could lead to a Bitcoin bull run. The analyst believes crypto and commodities are highly undervalued, noting that commodities were last seen at similar levels in 2000 and 1971.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCommodities & crypto are extremely undervalued, and it\u8217\'20\'19s likely that commodities go into a 10-year-long bull market. I\u8217\'20\'19m expecting a lot of upside from these two asset classes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A growing number of analysts anticipate a BTC breakout in October, with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s September 18 meeting acting as a potential catalyst. BTC is flashing signals hinting at a surge to the $100,000 and $150,000 range by 2025. This is because the cryptocurrency\u8217\'20\'19s recent price action displays an array of technical indicators aligning with a breakout. The most notable pattern on the chart is that of the \u8220\'20\'1Ccup and handle.\u8221\'20\'1D The cup and handle is a classical technical formation that suggests continued \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum.\par \par \uc2 Other indicators, such as BTC\u8217\'20\'19s weekly Bollinger Bands Width (BBW), have been contracting since June. This indicates low \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has preceded significant price movements. Momentum oscillators such as the Stochastic RSI and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  also hint at oversold conditions.\par \par \uc2 SEC Comes In For Criticism\par \par \uc2 The Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) came under criticism from \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Paul Grewal\uc2  and \uc2 Ripple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Stuart Aldertoy for its inconsistent and confusing approach to crypto asset regulations after it admitted it may have caused confusion by repeatedly stating that tokens are securities. Grewal highlighted a footnote from the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s amended complaint against Binance, which stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe SEC regrets any confusion it may have invited\u8217\'20\'19 by falsely and repeatedly stating that tokens themselves are securities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Responding to Grewal, \uc2 Ripple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal chief stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo the SEC finally admits that 1/\u8216\'20\'18crypto asset security\u8217\'20\'19 is a made up term and 2/ to prove a \u8216\'20\'18crypto asset security\u8217\'20\'19 is an investment contract, the SEC needs evidence of a bundle of \u8216\'20\'18contracts, expectations, and understandings\u8217\'20\'19? \uc2 Ripple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s case is over, but the \u8216\'20\'18fair notice\u8217\'20\'19 defense is still alive for others. The SEC cites the 2017 DAO report as industry notice that \u8216\'20\'18crypto asset securities\u8217\'20\'19 are subject to US securities laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/09/crypto-price-analysis-9-13-btc-eth-sol-wif-dot-tao-inj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  registered considerable movement last week and over the weekend, amassing a 6% increase as it climbed above $60,000. However, this jump was short-lived as BTC fell back, with the price down almost 3% over the past 24 hours. BTC was relatively positive over the previous week, recovering from a low of $52,622, which it fell to last Friday. By Monday (September 9), BTC was back above $57,000, with buyers pushing it to a day high of $58,092, testing the resistance at that level. Despite the positive start to the previous week, BTC could only push above $58,000 on Thursday, thanks to sellers actively defending the level, preventing buyers from pushing higher as demand dried up.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/9PpRJj1k/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 After facing significant selling pressure on Wednesday, BTC recovered strongly on Thursday as sellers pushed above $58,000 and settled at $58,176. Buyer sentiment picked up after BTC pushed above $58,000. As a result, Friday saw BTC move above the 20-day SMA and the 50-day SMA to go past $60,000 and settle at $60,479. Buyers were expected to defend the $60,000 level vigorously, and unsurprisingly, selling pressure increased over the weekend as sellers attempted to push BTC back below the 50-day SMA. BTC did not slip below the 50-day SMA on Saturday but lost the $60,000 level, declining by 0.88% and settling at $59,949. Sellers continued to dominate on Sunday, pushing BTC below the 50-day SMA as it dropped to $59,165. With markets opening in the red, the current session sees BTC down almost 1% as sellers look to lower the price.\par \par \uc2 BTC had slipped to a low of $58,143 early in the session. However, buyers pushed back, allowing BTC to climb to its current level of $58,762. Buyers will look to keep BTC above $58,000, counter selling pressure, and prevent a drop to $55,000. Should BTC recover during the ongoing session, we could see a retest of the $60,000 level. On the other hand, if sellers are successful in pushing BTC below $58,000, a drop back to $55,000 can be expected. Buyers have the upper hand with the MACD, which is currently \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that could change the longer sellers remain in control.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) continued its struggles as \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified over the weekend, pushing it to a low of $2,287 on Sunday. With markets in the red, ETH has remained in the red during the current session as sellers look to drive the price lower. The altcoin has been down over 5% over the past 24 hours as it looks to reclaim the $2,300 level. According to data from \uc2 TradingView\uc2 , ETH\u8217\'20\'19s price collapse has resulted in the ETH/BTC ratio dropping to its lowest level since April 2021, falling to 0.038 on September 16.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/evDU2Gu9/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH struggled to push above $2,400 last week despite making a strong recovery after dropping to a low of $2,150 last Friday, a level at which buyers thronged the market to push ETH higher. By Tuesday, ETH had recovered and risen to $2,389, but it fell back on Wednesday as the resistance at $2,400 came into play, and ETH saw active selling. Sellers attempted to drag ETH below $2,300 but could not do so, thanks to strong support. As a result, ETH recovered on Thursday, registering an increase of 0.91%, and settled at $2,363. ETH pushed $2,400 on Friday, registering an increase of 3.34% and settling at $2,442.\par \par \uc2 However, with the 20-day SMA coming into play, ETH fell back into the red over the weekend. ETH registered a 0.91% drop on Saturday and a substantial 4.21% drop on Sunday to slip back below $2,400 and settle at $2,318. The current session sees ETH down just over 1%, trading at $2,294. ETH has strong support at $2,300; buyers will look to reclaim this level to prevent further downside. However, if sellers continue to dominate, ETH could slip below $2,200 and drop to $2,150 or $2,100.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) has been down almost 5% over the past 24 hours after failure to push above $140. It was seen slip back into the red over the weekend, with sellers looking to drive it below $130. SOL was largely in the green last week after recovering from a low of $120, rebounding strongly to reclaim $130 by the beginning of last week, rising to $135. However, SOL faced considerable resistance and was unable to make any substantial push above this level, falling to a low of $128 on Wednesday before recovering on Thursday and settling at $136.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/EA2K76b5/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL faced intense selling pressure on Friday as it fell to a low of $131. However, it rebounded from this level, moving past the 20-day SMA and settling at $139 after an increase of 2.25%. However, with strong resistance at this level, SOL fell back into the red over the weekend, registering a 1.96% drop on Saturday. Selling pressure intensified on Sunday as SOL dropped over 4% to slip below the 20-day SMA and settle at $131.53. The current session sees SOL down marginally as sellers look to drive it below the $130 support level.\par \par \uc2 Buyers are expected to defend the $130 level and prevent a further decline. However, if SOL slips below this level, a decline to $120 can be expected.\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) registered an incredible increase of almost 14% over the past seven days, despite its upward push stalling over the weekend after encountering strong resistance around $6. TON was extremely \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week as it surged on Monday, reaching a day high of $5.69. However, buyers could not sustain momentum, and TON eventually settled at $5.25, registering an increase of 6.12%. TON surged past the 20-day SMA on Tuesday, rising by 5.65% and settling at $5.55. However, after encountering resistance, the price fell back on Wednesday, dropping to a low of $5.15 before recovering and settling at $5.39, back above the moving average.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/YKJio2Yp/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 TON attempted a move past the resistance at $5.60 on Thursday but eventually settled at $5.58 after an increase of 3.43%. It finally broke past this level on Friday, rising by 4.25% and settling at $5.81. Buyers attempted a move to $6 but lost momentum after reaching a high of $5.93, with the 50-day SMA coming into play as resistance. TON fell back over the weekend as demand dried up, dropping 2.38% on Saturday and 2.24% on Sunday to slip back below $5.60 and settle at $5.55. The current session sees TON up by 0.80% after sellers failed to lower the price. Buyers will look to reclaim $5.60. If TON can consolidate above this level, a push above the 50-day SMA to $6 could be possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if sellers retake control, TON could slip to $5.30, where the 20-day SMA could act as support. Should TON continue to drop, its next support level lies at $5.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) stalled over the weekend, as its impressive recovery was abruptly halted at $4.50, a level where it faces considerable resistance. DOT started the previous week on a positive note, rising to $4.29 on Monday after an increase of almost 3%. However, with the 20-day SMA coming into play, DOT turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dropping by 0.93% on Tuesday and tanking to a day low of $4.07 on Wednesday. However, DOT rebounded from this level, pushing above the 20-day SMA on Thursday and settling at $4.30 after registering an increase of 2.63%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/Aw1aSU0B/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT continued to push higher on Friday as it set its sights on $4.50, registering an increase of just over 3% to settle at $4.43. Sellers attempted to take control on Saturday as selling pressure grew. As a result, DOT dropped to a low of $4.35. Sellers lost momentum, allowing buyers to regain control, but with strong resistance at $4.50, DOT could register only a marginal increase and settle at $4.44. Buyers lost steam on Sunday after a push above $4.50 failed to materialize. DOT fell back into the red after reaching a high of $4.56, as sellers drove the price back down. It eventually settled at $4.40 after a drop of 0.90%.\par \par \uc2 As seen in the price chart, sellers attempted to drive DOT below the 20-day SMA during the current session. As a result, DOT fell to a low of $4.24 before recovering and climbing to its current level of $4.34. Buyers will look to regain control of the session and test the $4.50 level once again. On the other hand, sellers will look to push DOT down to $4, but first, they will have to overcome potential support at the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) continues to trade in a narrow range, with neither buyers nor sellers able to dictate the session. As a result, WIF has oscillated between $1.50 and $1.70 for most of the previous week. WIF dropped to a day low of $1.49 on Wednesday but quickly recovered. By Friday, it had risen above the 20-day SMA to settle at $1.63 after an increase of just over 5%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/WUtqHYzg/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, WIF had been facing significant resistance at $1.60, and with a downward-sloping 50-day SMA coming into play, it fell back into the red on Saturday, dropping over 4% to slip below $1.60 once again and settle at $1.56. The price continued to drop on Sunday as WIF registered a drop of 4.19% to slip below the 20-day SMA and settle at $1.50. The current session sees WIF up by just over 1% as buyers look to push it back toward $1.60.\par \par \uc2 Ripple\uc2  (XRP) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 The past week, \uc2 Ripple\uc2  (XRP) saw a substantial surge, allowing it to push above a crucial resistance level and the 20, 50, and 200-day SMAs. XRP had dipped to a low of $0.50 last Friday before rebounding and starting a steady recovery, reaching $0.53 by Tuesday. After registering a drop of just over 1% on Wednesday, XRP registered a sharp uptick on Thursday, pushing above the 20 and 200-day SMAs to settle at $0.56. A 1.99% increase on Friday saw XRP push above the 50-day SMA and settle at $0.57.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/fjk8U23Z/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP started the weekend on a positive note, registering an increase of 3.92% to move to $0.59, as buyers looked to push above $0.60. However, strong selling pressure at this level saw XRP fall back into the red on Sunday, ending the weekend at $0.57 after a drop of 4.04%. The current session sees XRP marginally up as buyers and sellers look to establish control. Buyers will look to keep XRP above the 50-day SMA. Should XRP consolidate above it, we could see a retest of the resistance at $0.60. On their part, sellers will look to drive XRP below $0.55.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240917ek9g0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Tokens\par \b \uc2 New tokens are more likely to win if they find institutional investors\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yat Siu \par \uc2 1,267 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Most of the new tokens launched in 2024 have fared poorly compared to their predecessors. However, institutional investment has helped some succeed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWZjMjQtODkyZS03ZTIwLTkxMzMtNDE4MWNhMWFkZWQw.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New tokens are more likely to win if they find institutional investors}}}\par \par \uc2 The market capitalization of all fungible tokens stands at more than $2 trillion as of Sept. 16. Of that total, altcoins \u8212\'20\'14 cryptocurrencies other than Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) \u8212\'20\'14 have gained around $240 billion in combined market value over the last 12 months.\par \par \uc2 Despite this powerful overall growth, the majority of new tokens launched in 2024 have performed poorly and failed to gain sufficient traction. Why haven\u8217\'20\'19t new tokens gained value in a manner similar to their predecessors? One word: attention. The market cap for altcoins is up because it comprises a stunning number of new tokens that were launched in 2024. However, this abundance of tokens has also greatly diluted attention for individual altcoins, causing fragmented liquidity that in turn produces weak price performance post-listing.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fc47-9436-7ecb-adae-ea7dca63791c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New tokens are more likely to win if they find institutional investors}}}\par \par \uc2 Increase in market capitalization for Bitcoin and Ethereum between September 2023 and September 2024. Source: Animoca Labs\par \par \uc2 The market cap of altcoins grew by more than 70% in one year, which is in line with the two main cryptocurrencies. The obvious difference is that, while Bitcoin and Ether are single currencies, there are millions of different altcoins, each contributing to the altcoin market cap. The dominance of bitcoin and ether (the market share of those cryptocurrencies compared against altcoins) remained fairly stable throughout the year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fc48-fc30-725a-9ef2-1521467df6a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New tokens are more likely to win if they find institutional investors}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin market dominance from November 2023 through September 2024. Source: CoinMarketCap\par \par \uc2 But on an individual level, most altcoins launched in 2024 performed poorly. Much of the discussion about this problem has focused on the negative impact on token value resulting from excessively high {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/its-time-to-bring-back-low-fdv-token-sales-and-fair-community-launches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fully-diluted values (FDVs)}}}\uc2  and low circulating supply, or the divide between venture capital and retail investors. However, at least one analysis \u8212\'20\'14 by Dragonfly Managing Partner Haseeb Qureshi \u8212\'20\'14 found insufficient evidence to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/hosseeb/status/1792257063399403669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conclude}}}\uc2  that the poor performance of altcoins in 2024 could be ascribed to those factors.\par \par \uc2 In a saturated market, attention is the new currency\par \par \uc2 The total number of altcoins has increased by 107% in one year, growing from 1.69 million tokens as of August 2023 to over 3.5 million tokens today. In stark contrast, the crypto user base has grown far less rapidly over the same period. Global crypto ownership {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20240913074627/https://www.triple-a.io/cryptocurrency-ownership-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  by 33% from 2023 to 2023 \u8212\'20\'14 from 420 million people to 562 million.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/starknet-ditching-off-chain-polling-to-make-tokens-count"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starknet is ditching offchain polling, and it will make tokens count}}}\par \par \uc2 So we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at a situation in which the offering of altcoins has more than doubled while the addressable audience increased only by a third. Consumer attention has been greatly diluted.\par \par \uc2 This abundance of altcoins and the resulting dilution of attention are not particularly unusual in a growing market. For example, in the early days of the Web, a veritable plethora of IRC chat rooms, message boards and websites sprang up, all of them competing for traffic and diluting the attention of a burgeoning audience.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s profusion of altcoins means that awareness has become a highly competitive matter for all altcoins, not just new ones \u8212\'20\'14 tokens launched prior to 2024 have also suffered a dilution in attention and (consequently) value.\par \par \uc2 Tokens with institutional investors outperform the competition\par \par \uc2 Well-performing tokens in 2024 tend to have significant institutional interest from liquid funds. Liquid institutional investors invest via the open market, as opposed to investing at the startup stage the way that VC firms do, and as such can have a notable impact on the performance of altcoins. Altcoins such as TON ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/toncoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TON}}}\uc2  ), \uc2 SOL\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ), BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), TRX ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tron-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TRX}}}\uc2  ), AVAX ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ), SUI ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/sui-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SUI}}}\uc2  ), and MOCA are examples of tokens with institutional support.\par \par \uc2 That support can help altcoins to offset the dilution of attention in a teeming market. Institutions are discerning and disciplined in how they invest, and try to zero in on fundamental long-term prospects rather than investing in short-term outlooks such as those of many altcoins (and definitely most memecoins). This institutional participation makes an altcoin stand out from the crowd and instills greater confidence among retail investors. As opposed to the current environment of diluted attention and fragmented liquidity, institutional liquid funds could bring improved attention, focus and liquidity to altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/choke-point-continues-to-hurt-kamala-harris-crypto-reset"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Choke Point 2.0 is hurting Kamala Harris' 'crypto reset'}}}\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors also have the capacity to deploy significantly more capital and on a longer time horizon than retail investors, and this can contribute to enhancing price stability in the market. Altcoins that lack institutional support tend to be subject to greater \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Animoca Brands\uc2 , we have provided institutional support for projects and initiatives including by participating in the \uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stablecoin issuer sandbox (with Standard Chartered and HKT); partnering with Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s NEOM; investing in TON; and investing in Mocaverse \u8212\'20\'14 specifically with MOCA Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s launch of MOCA Coin, has received support from other institutional investors. Our aim is to equip our supported projects with essential capabilities. We have also expanded our investment mandate to include tokens already listed, with an emphasis on tokens from our portfolio of Web3 investments.\par \par \uc2 The current market presents significant opportunities for launched altcoins with solid institutional appeal and capability, and they stand a far greater chance of success amid the shifting market dynamics.\par \par \uc2 There is room for more institutional investment\par \par \uc2 There is room for institutional investment in crypto to grow. Institutional investors dominate the US equity market, where they hold 80% of the large-cap S&P 500\u8217\'20\'19s market capitalization. This contrasts strongly with the more diversified Web3 market, where the institutional footprint is still low and concentrated on Bitcoin. As of June, 77% of institutional asset managers had allocated just 5% or less of their funds to cryptocurrencies and related assets, with a preference for registered vehicles.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fc5c-9943-71d4-8119-e6d4b4cbcbc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New tokens are more likely to win if they find institutional investors}}}\par \par \uc2 EY-Parthenon research estimates the percentage of fund allocation into cryptocurrencies, digital assets, and related crypto funds/products. Source: EY-Parthenon\par \par \uc2 Consider that Bitcoin's market cap is around $1.1 trillion \u8212\'20\'14 while Bitcoin ETFs represent less than $80 billion. This disparity highlights both the need and the opportunity for Web3 to foster a more balanced market, one where institutional holdings might reach around 50% of the Web3 market.\par \par \uc2 Greater institutional participation could engender greater trust in Web3 projects while introducing substantial new long-term capital. Web3 projects that are capable of attracting institutional interest will stand out in this crowded market, providing one important pathway to overcoming the problem of attention dilution. We believe that financial institutions are essential in Web3, just as they are in other industries, and Web3 projects that seek meaningful long-term success would be well advised to pursue strategies that enable them to secure institutional participation.\par \par \uc2 Yat Siu\uc2  is a guest columnist for Cointelegraph and the co-founder and executive chairman of \uc2 Animoca Brands\uc2 , a Web3 leader with more than 540 investments in the sector.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWZjMjQtODkyZS03ZTIwLTkxMzMtNDE4MWNhMWFkZWQw.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240916ek9g000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 BTC\par \b \uc2 Crypto investment products see $436M inflow, while Ethereum continues to suffer\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Nancy Lubale \par \uc2 546 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Crypto investment products saw a notable uptick in inflows, but Ethereum flows remain negative.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWZiZmQtMGM4OC03NzQwLThkODQtNjAyMTE5M2YyOWEw.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto investment products see $436M inflow, while Ethereum continues to suffer}}}\par \par \uc2 According to the latest report by \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 , flows into cryptocurrency investment products rebounded last week, with $436 million in net inflows led by Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Following a two-week streak of outflows, crypto funds at asset managers such as \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , Bitwise, \uc2 Fidelity\uc2 , Grayscale, \uc2 ProShares\uc2  and \uc2 21Shares\uc2  saw positive flows for the week ending Sept. 13 in what \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  believes can be explained by the market\u8217\'20\'19s expectation of an interest rate cut by the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the latest \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly Report,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  head of research James Butterfill wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe the surge in inflows toward the end of the week was driven by a significant shift in market expectations for a potential 50 basis point interest rate cut on September 18th.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbe9-5c85-7f00-bbe0-5c35aec2edb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto investment products see $436M inflow, while Ethereum continues to suffer}}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CoinSharesCo/status/1835685570867061070"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinShares}}}\par \par \uc2 However, Butterfill added that trading volumes in crypto investment products remained flat for the week at $8 billion, much lower than the $14.2 billion average for 2024.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin investment products dominate as Ether struggles\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) investment products led the reversal, seeing $436 million in inflows after seeing a 10-day run of outflows totaling $1.8 billion, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  explained.\par \par \uc2 Short Bitcoin investment product flows also reversed, registering net outflows of $8.5 million following three consecutive weeks of inflows.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbea-7dda-7111-9cb1-6b710082d3c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto investment products see $436M inflow, while Ethereum continues to suffer}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto investment products flows by asset. Source: \uc2 CoinShares\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) investment products also witnessed net inflows of $3.8 million last week \u8212\'20\'14 the fourth week in a row. \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) also saw inflows totaling $300,000 and $600,000, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/spot-bitcoin-etfs-hackers-risk-caroline-ellison-ftx-prison-hodlers-digest/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin ETFs may face hacker threats, Ellison seeks no prison time, and more: Hodler\u8217\'20\'19s Digest, Sept. 8\u8211\'20\'1314}}}\par \par \uc2 However, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinued to suffer,\u8221\'20\'1D experiencing $19 million in outflows during the Sept. 9 to Sept. 13 week, adding to $98 million in negative flows the previous week. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  believes this is due to concerns over the profitability of the layer-1 blockchain following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/what-is-the-ethereum-dencun-upgrade-and-why-is-it-important#:~:text=The%20upgrade%20is%20set%20to,the%20state%20of%20the%20blockchain."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dencun upgrade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some traders say the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/spot-bitcoin-etfs-see-highest-flow-day-in-over-5-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant flows into spot Bitcoin exchange-traded funds (ETFs)}}}\uc2  since their market debut on Jan. 11 compared to Ether ETFs experiencing net outflows have swung investor preference toward Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 This has seen the ETH/BTC ratio drop below $0.04, the lowest level since April 2021.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbeb-21be-774a-8dca-f1f2471b8e09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto investment products see $436M inflow, while Ethereum continues to suffer}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/BTC weekly chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 Since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/spot-ethereum-etfs-surpass-1-billion-trading-volume-on-day-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 going live on July 23}}}\uc2 , Ether ETFs have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sosovalue.xyz/assets/etf/us-eth-spot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recorded}}}\uc2  net outflows of $581 million. In comparison, spot Bitcoin ETFs took on over $12 billion in their first two months and have recorded over $17 billion in net inflows in just over eight months of trading.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbeb-959c-744e-9dae-e8348bbf7835"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto investment products see $436M inflow, while Ethereum continues to suffer}}}\par \par \uc2 Spot Ethereum ETF cumulative flow. Source: Farside Investors\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWZiZmQtMGM4OC03NzQwLThkODQtNjAyMTE5M2YyOWEw.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240916ek9g000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , XRP, DOGE, TON,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,615 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s fall below $58,000 shows that the bulls are cautious before the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s rate cut announcement on Sept. 18.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWZiYmItMjZlNC03MDMwLWEwMmMtNmQzZTI1OTU0ZDhi.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) failure to maintain above the psychologically crucial $60,000 level shows that buying dries up at higher levels. The nervousness could be due to the uncertainty regarding the extent of the rate cut by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  on Sept. 18 and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-bitcoin-price-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subsequent reaction by the markets}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe the rate cuts will be \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the crypto markets. Trading firm QCP Capital told its Telegram channel subscribers to prepare for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-60k-double-breakout-zone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complementary scenarios for risk assets and cryptocurrencies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite some short-term uncertainty and potential drawdowns, we still favor locking in yields ahead of the rates cut and positioning for \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  scenarios,\u8221\'20\'1D the firm said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbb6-5112-7bba-b18e-5948c9449a7a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 However, not everyone is positive about the rate cut. A few believe that an aggressive rate cut signals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/markets-see-0-5-fed-rate-cut-5-things-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deeper concerns in the economy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, sharp cuts have preceded recessions. Why? It shows the government is scared and scrambling to reverse an overreach,\u8221\'20\'1D financial analyst and investor Jacob King, CEO of crypto newsletter WhaleWire, told his X followers.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin continue lower and retest the $55,724 support? Will that increase selling in select altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index recovered strongly last week and is near the all-time high of 5,670, indicating sustained buying by the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbb6-f9e3-709c-96ac-f91926ef8be7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will have to guard the overhead resistance with all their might because if they fail in their endeavor, the index could resume the uptrend and rally toward the next target objective of 6,000.\par \par \uc2 On the downside, the first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the moving averages. Selling could pick up further if the index breaks and sustains below 5,400. That could signal a range formation between 5,100 and 5,670.\par \par \uc2 US Dollar Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The US Dollar Index (DXY) has been in a downtrend for several days. Generally, in a downtrend, traders sell the rallies to the 20-day exponential moving average (101.54), and that is what happened on Sept. 12.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbb7-d3c8-7fe4-bf72-573f07311fe0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to strengthen their position by pulling the price below the 100.50 support. If they manage to do that, the index could slide to 99.57, which is likely to attract strong buying by the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Buyers will have to drive and maintain the price above the overhead resistance of 102 to suggest that the downtrend may be ending. The index could attempt a rally to 103.50 and then to 105.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has pulled back below the 20-day EMA ($58,338) on Sept. 16, indicating that the bears are applying pressure.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbb8-c2b0-7b96-8abf-955fab4f28bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns up from the current levels, the bulls will make one more attempt to drive the BTC/USDT pair above $61,200. If they succeed, the pair could start a rally to $65,000. A break and close above $65,000 will negate the lower highs formation on the pair, which is a positive sign.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, a close below the 20-day EMA could tug the price to the vital support zone between $55,724 and $52,550.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($2,414) on Sept. 15 and dropped to the solid support near $2,300.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbb9-a33c-75a6-bed0-c5723cffd077"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The down sloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (\uc2 RSI\uc2 ) in the negative zone indicate that the bears have an edge. If the price continues lower and closes below $2,300, the slide could extend to $2,111. A break and close below this support could signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a rally above the moving averages. The ETH/USDT pair could then climb to the breakdown level of $2,850. Buyers will have to overcome this resistance to suggest a trend change.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been trading between $460 and $635 for several months, indicating buying near the support and selling close to the resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbbb-81f6-7c26-8389-617c96949191"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to pull the price below the moving averages. If they can pull it off, the BNB/USDT pair could slump toward $460.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns up from the moving averages, it will suggest that the short-term sentiment has turned positive. The pair could rise to $600 and then to $635. Sellers are expected to fiercely defend the zone between $600 and $635, but if the bulls prevail, the pair may run up to $722.\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) rose above the 20-day EMA ($135) on Sept. 13, but the bulls could not maintain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbbc-25f5-7f06-8c03-fe7ee1c62e44"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down and slipped below the 20-day EMA on Sept. 15. The bears will try to sink the price to the critical support of $116, where the buyers are likely to step in and arrest the decline.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated in the near term if the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair turns up and breaks above the 50-day simple moving average ($143). That could start a recovery to the overhead resistance of $164, which may be a formidable barrier for the bulls to cross.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been swinging inside a large range between $0.41 and $0.64 for several weeks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbbc-f019-71ec-9cd6-b437a27f4378"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages have flattened out, and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  is near the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. The bulls will have to push the price above the $0.64 resistance to take charge.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price continues lower and breaks below the uptrend line, it will suggest that the short-term advantage has tilted in favor of the bears. That could sink the XRP/USDT pair to $0.50 and eventually to $0.46.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-happened-in-crypto-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today}}}\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Buyers are finding it difficult to push Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line of the falling wedge pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbbe-2da6-7437-8c19-51a29ec6f2b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price maintains below the 20-day EMA ($0.10), it will suggest that the bulls have given up. The DOGE/USDT pair could then sink to $0.09. This is an important level for the bulls to protect because a break below it will tilt the advantage in favor of the bears. The pair could then plunge to $0.08.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns up and breaks above the downtrend line, it will signal a potential trend change. The pair may rally to $0.14 and thereafter to $0.18.\par \par \uc2 Toncoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/toncoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TON}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 50-day SMA ($5.87) on Sept. 14, indicating that the bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbc2-3b1c-7f0f-a223-14c6d50c45f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 TON/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to defend the 20-day EMA ($5.44) if they want to start a sustained recovery. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA and breaks above the 50-day SMA, it will suggest that the buyers have the upper hand. The TON/USDT pair could climb to $7, where the rally may hit a hurdle.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the 20-day EMA breaks down, the pair is likely to retest the crucial support near $4.72. A break and close below $4.44 could start a new downtrend toward $3.50.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) slipped back below the moving averages on Sept. 15, indicating that the bears have kept up the pressure.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191fbc1-711d-7f3f-a6ac-304fda107bc1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/16: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair is forming a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  descending triangle pattern, which will complete on a break and close below the crucial support at $0.31. That could start a downward move toward the next major support at $0.24.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to push and maintain the price above the downtrend line to invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The pair could rally to $0.40 and subsequently to $0.46, where the bears may mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2l