\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 9-3 BTC, ETH, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOGE, DOT, UNI,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Analysts Warn BTC Could See 20% Dip}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A Turbulent Month Ahead}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC Exchange Reserves Hit Multi-Year Low}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 ) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) has climbed back above $59,000 during the ongoing session, reaching a high of $59,764 and registering an increase of almost 3% over the past 24 hours. However, analysts are worried September could see BTC dip to $45,000, putting it on a path culminating at $40,000.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin struggled in August, with suggestions that the price could see a further 5% dip. BTC has traded in the red for six of the last seven September months. Other major cryptocurrencies also registered gains, with Ethereum (ETH) climbing back above $2,500. \uc2 Solana\uc2  (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) moved back above $130 and is currently trading around the $135 mark, while Dogecoin (DOGE) could look to reclaim the $0.100 price level.\par \par \uc2 Analysts Warn BTC Could See 20% Dip\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Bitfinex\uc2  have warned that Bitcoin (BTC) could dip by as much as 20% because the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s upcoming rate cut decision introduces a degree of uncertainty in the market. The prediction was made in a research report published on September 2, with the analysts attributing BTC\u8217\'20\'19s recent 32% surge to speculations surrounding a dovish Fed stance. However, the report also outlined that the anticipated September rate cut could significantly influence BTC\u8217\'20\'19s short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and long-term trajectory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA 25 basis point cut is likely to signal the beginning of a typical easing cycle, which could lead to long-term price appreciation for Bitcoin as liquidity increases and recession fears ease.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the event of a more aggressive 50 basis point cut, BTC could see an immediate jump in price followed by a correction as concerns around a recession escalate. Market dynamics have shifted over the past week, with spot holders de-risking and perpetual market speculators attempting to buy the dip, which is seen in significant long open interest in BTC perpetuals.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, global crypto investment products have registered $305 million in weekly outflows, according to data from \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 . The net outflows of last week are in stark contrast with net inflows worth $543 million seen a week prior. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  Head of Research James Butterfill stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe outflows came amid \u8220\'20\'1Cwidespread negative sentiment evident across various providers and regions, driven by stronger-than-expected economic data in the U.S., which \u8220\'20\'1Cdiminished the likelihood of a 50-basis point interest rate cut. We continue to expect the asset class to become increasingly sensitive to interest rate expectations as the Fed gets closer to a pivot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A Turbulent Month Ahead\par \par \uc2 Analysts predict that BTC could see a substantial decline following a rate cut, with a potential bottom between $40,000 and $50,000. The forecast is based on historical data showing that percentage return peaks typically dip by 60-70% each cycle, along with a reduction in average bull market corrections. September has historically been a difficult month for BTC, with an average return of -4.78% and peak-to-trough declines of around 24.6%. According to analysts, this \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the risk of a \u8220\'20\'1Csell-the-news\u8221\'20\'1D reaction following the rate cut could present traders with opportunities and risks.\par \par \uc2 BTC Exchange Reserves Hit Multi-Year Low\par \par \uc2 BTC reserves on exchanges have hit a multi-year low, with crypto exchanges now holding just 2.39 million BTC, significantly lower than the 2020 peak. BTC\u8217\'20\'19s current price sits just under the $59,000 mark, down over 6% in the past week as ETFs see continuous outflows. According to Kristian Haralampiev, Structured Products Lead at Nexo, the drop in BTC prices can be attributed to anxiety surrounding the upcoming release of the U.S. non-farm payroll data and its potential impact on the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting looming, investors are bracing for new economic data that could significantly influence the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe BTC is in a consolidation phase and could repeat a bull run and hit a new all-time high.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin \u8211\'20\'13 Bull run 2.0 Incoming. The current monthly consolidation on BTC looks a lot like the previous cycle when the price surged all the way to its all-time high.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/09/crypto-price-analysis-9-2-btc-eth-sol-dot-ton-atom-wif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  is clearly in a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend since hitting a peak of over $66,000 on July 29, consistently making lower highs and lower lows, indicating considerable market weakness. While BTC did reach a high of $65,000 on August 23, it has since dipped below $60,000 and the 20, 50, and 200-day SMAs, indicating growing \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment, and has since struggled to reclaim $60,000 or register a positive price movement. BTC dipped below the 20-day SMA last week when it registered a drop of 5.39% and fell to $59,509. Buyers attempted a move back above the moving average and $60,000 on Wednesday but could not do so as sellers took control and pushed BTC down to $59,085.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/BdIVG8Tw/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Another attempt to reclaim $60,000 was made on Thursday as BTC reached a high of $61,230. However, buyers lost momentum again, and BTC fell below $60,000 and settled at $59,436 after registering a marginal increase. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure increased substantially as the weekend rolled in, with the price dropping to a day low of $57,733 on Friday before recovering and rising to $59,163. Saturday saw yet another marginal drop and a 2.62% drop on Sunday ensured that BTC ended the previous week on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note at $57,399. Thanks to strong demand near the $57,000 price level, BTC started the current week on a positive note, registering an increase of just over 3% to move back above $59,000 and settle at $59,169.\par \par \uc2 The current session has already seen buyers attempt to push above the 20-day SMA. However, sellers have thwarted the move for now, with the price down marginally, although still above $59,000.\par \par \uc2 With the moving averages positioned above the current price, market trends hint at growing bearishness, with the MACD also currently \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Sellers will continue their efforts to overwhelm the support around $57,000. If this level is breached, BTC could drop to $55,000 or below. BTC must push above the 20-day SMA and the $60,000 price level for any upward price movement.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) has registered an increase of almost 3% over the past 24 hours, although it remains in the red if we look at weekly price movements. The world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest cryptocurrency has been trading between $2,400 and $2,600 since August 27, when it dipped below the 20-day SMA and settled at $2,458. Thanks to strong buying demand around $2,400, ETH rebounded the following day, pushing back above $2,500 and settling at $2,529. However, buyers lost steam on Thursday after reaching a high of $2,597, with sellers forcing ETH back down to $2,529. Sellers attempted to overwhelm the $2,400 support level on Friday as ETH dropped to a low of $2,437 but buyers could push ETH back above $2,500, and it eventually settled at $2,527.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/OQXFgu0b/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Sellers assumed control over the weekend as ETH dropped by 0.49% on Saturday and 3.44% on Sunday to end the previous week at $2,438, again losing the crucial $2,500 price level. Once again, strong support around the $2,400 level allowed buyers to push ETH up substantially on Monday. As a result, ETH registered a jump of 4.55% to move to $2,539. The current session sees ETH marginally down as sellers attempt to drive the price back below $2,500.\par \par \uc2 So, where does ETH go from here? With the price losing key support levels and unable to push above resistance levels, ETH is currently stuck between $2,400 and $2,600. If sellers breach the $2,400 level, ETH could dip to $2,200 or $2,100. However, if buyers can keep ETH above $2,500 and engineer a push above $2,600, it would indicate the bears are losing grip. A close above $2,600 could set ETH up for a push toward the crucial $2,850 price level.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) has been extremely \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  since being rejected from the $160 price level on August 24. Since then, it has dipped below the 20, 50, and 200-day SMAs. In fact, \uc2 SOL\uc2  spent all of last week in the red, dropping to $142 by Thursday. Sellers attempted to drag \uc2 SOL\uc2  below $130 on Friday as the price dipped to a low of $132. However, demand picked up close to $130, allowing \uc2 SOL\uc2  to push back to $138. Despite attempts to counter selling pressure, \uc2 SOL\uc2  lost the $140 price level, ending Friday with a 1.46% decline.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/plJlGqQg/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Selling pressure intensified on Saturday and Sunday as \uc2 SOL\uc2  registered drops of 1.90% and 5.03% on Saturday and Sunday, respectively. As a result, \uc2 SOL\uc2  dipped below the crucial $130 price level to end the weekend at $128. Buyers were always expected to defend this level, and sure enough, \uc2 SOL\uc2  recovered as Monday rolled in, registering an increase of 4.98% to reclaim the $130 level and settle at $135. The current session sees \uc2 SOL\uc2  marginally down as buyers and sellers attempt to assert influence and dictate price movements. If \uc2 SOL\uc2  can maintain its position above $130, bulls will attempt to retake $140 and push to $145-$150. Should \uc2 SOL\uc2  reclaim $150, the next resistance level sits at $160.\par \par \uc2 However, if sellers control the session, \uc2 SOL\uc2  could dip back below $130. In such a situation, bears will try to drag the price below $120 and test the $116 support level.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) has traded between $0.090 and $0.100 since slipping below the 20-day SMA on Wednesday (August 27). Since then, neither buyers nor sellers have been able to exert influence, with DOGE registering only a marginal increase on Thursday and Friday. Sellers attempted to push DOGE below $0.100 on Friday as the price dropped to a low of $0.097. However, buyers countered the selling pressure and pushed DOGE up by 1.39% to $0.101. Despite DOGE seeing an uptick, buyers lost momentum as the resistance at the 20-day SMA came into play.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/RvHITexy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 As a result, DOGE fell by 0.88% on Saturday to close at $0.100. Selling pressure intensified on Sunday as liquidity dried up, resulting in DOGE dropping almost 6%, slipping below $0.100 and settling at $0.095. Buyers returned to the market on Monday, pushing DOGE up by 3.78% to $0.098. The current session sees DOGE up just over 1% as buyers attempt to reclaim $0.100. If buyers fail to reclaim $0.100, it would indicate that sellers have the upper hand. In such a scenario, DOGE could drop to $0.095 or as low as $0.090. However, should DOGE reclaim $0.100, it could push up to the next resistance level at $0.110.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) has staged an admirable recovery after facing considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment that dragged its price to a low of $4.04 and opened up the risk of a drop below $4. DOT had been in the red since failing to push above $5 on August 24. As sentiment flipped, DOT dropped below the 20-day SMA at the start of the previous week and slipped below the $4.50 price level by Tuesday. DOT dropped to $4.25 by Thursday after buyers failed to build momentum. Sellers attempted to push DOT below $4 on Friday as the price dipped to a low of $4.10, but with solid support at lower levels, buyers countered the selling pressure, allowing DOT to register a 0.94% increase and settle at $4.29.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/eYOqzYKB/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, DOT fell back into the red over the weekend, registering a marginal drop on Saturday. Sellers tested DOT\u8217\'20\'19s support level again on Sunday as DOT fell by 4.46% to close at $4.07. Once again, DOT\u8217\'20\'19s support held, and the price rebounded on Monday, rising by 3.44% to $4.21. The current session sees DOT up by 1.43%, trading just below the $4.30 mark. DOT\u8217\'20\'19s jump can be attributed to a surge in buyer interest following Polkadot announcing a partnership with Inter Miami Football Club. The partnership focuses on fan engagement and highlights the potential of Web3 technologies in sports.\par \par \uc2 Can DOT sustain its upward momentum? If buyers can push DOT back above the 20-day SMA, it means bulls are gaining momentum. In such a scenario, DOT could resume its push toward $5. DOT has strong support around the $4 level, which has already been tested twice, demonstrating that sellers are losing steam at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) dipped below the 20-day SMA on August 27 when it went below $6 and settled at $5.71. Since then, UNI steadily pushed back towards $6, reaching $5.90 by Friday despite sellers attempting to drag the price towards the $5.50 support level. Buyers retained control on Saturday and tried to push above $6 once more, reaching a day high of $0.09. However, buyers lost momentum, allowing sellers to push UNI back below $6 to $5.94, with the price only registering a marginal increase.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/HWEAjdU7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI fell into the red on Sunday as sellers took control, driving the price down by 5.55% to $5.61. Once again, sellers lost momentum at lower levels, allowing buyers to mount a recovery on Monday. As a result, UNI registered a significant jump of almost 9%, allowing it to break above $6 and settle at $6.11. The current session sees UNI up by 1.29% as buyers attempt to push the price above the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has continued to drop since failing to push above $0.40 on August 24, losing key support levels. Buyers attempted to counter the selling pressure after \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped below the moving average, attempting a recovery on Wednesday, as seen in the price chart. However, sellers pushed the price back down from a day high of $0.361 to $0.35. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  registered a 2.29% increase on Thursday to move above the 20-day SMA and settle at $0.358. Sellers thwarted attempts to push higher.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/JXrXzcpB/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned on Friday after \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped by just over 3%, slipping back below the 20-day SMA and settling at $0.347. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained in the red over the weekend, registering a marginal drop on Saturday and an almost 4% drop on Sunday to slip to $0.332, going below a crucial support level. The current week began with a 1.20% increase, but the price has fallen back into the red during the ongoing session and is currently down by almost 2.50%, trading at $0.328.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240904ek930000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cardano\par \b \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after \uc2 Charles Hoskinson\uc2  questioned BTC longevity\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 611 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 's price versus Bitcoin could drop by another 25% in 2025 after breaking below a lifetime support level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWI2Y2ItMTNkMy03ZjE3LTliZGMtMWFhNTE3YTIyNjdk.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after Charles Hoskinson questioned BTC longevity}}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) prices have not reacted positively each time in recent years after \uc2 Charles Hoskinson\uc2  mentioned something negative about Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  price down 75% since Hoskinson criticized BTC\par \par \uc2 Notably, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC trading pair has declined by 75% almost two years after Hoskinson questioned Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s survivability in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-founder-points-out-flaws-in-ethereum-and-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Cointelegraph}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the October 2022 conversation, Hoskinson argued that BTC should not be used on the Bitcoin blockchain network but on faster blockchains like Cardano or Ethereum as a wrapped asset.\par \par \uc2 At that time, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC was trading for as high as 2,188 satoshis (1 satoshi equals 0.00000001 BTC). But as of Sept. 3, the pair had declined to as low as 562 satoshis, closer to its lowest levels since December 2020.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b6c8-f7a5-781d-8612-7b111bd84f48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after Charles Hoskinson questioned BTC longevity}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC weekly price chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC\u8217\'20\'19s negative reaction to Hoskinson\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin criticism is part of a consistent pattern. In most cases, his remarks have been followed by declines in \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC, whether in the short or in the medium term.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b6ee-a1ee-7eef-8a48-239ca6620f1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after Charles Hoskinson questioned BTC longevity}}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/TuurDemeester/status/1830640199098884482"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\par \par \uc2 That was the case after Hoskinson\u8217\'20\'19s June 2021 critique, in which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/IOHK_Charles/status/1405189568916193283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likened}}}\uc2  Bitcoin to a \u8220\'20\'1Cwashed-up football star,\u8221\'20\'1D his April 2024 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HDUFalwgxEU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparison of Bitcoin to religion}}}\uc2 , his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cryptodotnew/status/1793671239992803717"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 2024 claim}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe industry doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need Bitcoin anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D or his June 2024 assertion that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QsIXBrHWqvM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano would surpass Bitcoin}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b6e3-6f6a-74c2-a0e9-d667509064c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after Charles Hoskinson questioned BTC longevity}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC monthly price chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC has crashed by almost 94% compared to its all-time high in January 2018.\par \par \uc2 Is \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  bottoming out versus BTC at last?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interim technical setup versus BTC looks skewed toward bulls.\par \par \uc2 Notably, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC pair is trading inside what appears to be a falling wedge setup, which traditional analysts consider a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal pattern. As a rule, a falling wedge setup resolves when the price breaks decisively above its upper trendline and rises by as much as the wedge\u8217\'20\'19s maximum height.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-chang-hard-fork-successful-shifts-decentralized-governance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s Chang hard fork successful as it shifts to decentralized governance}}}\par \par \uc2 Applying the same principle to the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC chart brings its falling wedge target to around 694 satoshis if the breakpoint point is where the pattern\u8217\'20\'19s trendlines converge. In other words, the pair could rally by approximately 25% by the end of 2024.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b748-11e8-75d3-996d-caa50ce19c43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after Charles Hoskinson questioned BTC longevity}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC daily price chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, on the longer-timeframe chart, a rebound does not necessarily indicate an \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC bottom.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b74a-f5dd-7826-8891-94230cea5b7c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano down 75% vs. Bitcoin 2 years after Charles Hoskinson questioned BTC longevity}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC six-week performance chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 Notably, the pair has dropped below its lifetime ascending trendline support in May 2024\u8212\'20\'14right after Hoskinson\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cthe industry doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need Bitcoin anymore\u8221\'20\'1D remark\u8212\'20\'14and has been constantly declining since.\par \par \uc2 Further drops could have \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  test the 1.0 Fibonacci retracement level at around 413 satoshis as the next downside target in 2025, down about 25% from current prices.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWI2Y2ItMTNkMy03ZjE3LTliZGMtMWFhNTE3YTIyNjdk.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240903ek930008h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
