\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 9-2 BTC, ETH, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOT, TON, ATOM, WIF\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 3,020 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Markets Await US Job Data}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where Do BTC And Other Altcoins Go From Here?}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Markets Lost Over $300 Million In August}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 First Crypto Transaction Between AI Agents}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toncoin (TON) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cosmos (ATOM) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Major cryptocurrencies are starting the new week in the red, with Bitcoin (BTC) tumbling below $58,000 and Ethereum (ETH) slipping below $2,500 once again. The overall crypto market cap also registered a drop of 1.91%, leaving it just above the $2 trillion mark.\par \par \uc2 Almost all cryptocurrencies have registered substantial weekly drops, with BTC down over 10%, ETH down almost 11%, and Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) down a staggering 20%. Other altcoins that registered substantial losses include Dogecoin (DOGE), which is down 14%; Toncoin (TON), down 10.71%; Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), down almost 15%; and Polkadot (DOT), down nearly 15% as well. Analysts now worry BTC could be heading for a bear market, with price action indicating a further decline.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Markets Await US Job Data\par \par \uc2 The traditional and cryptocurrency markets are holding their breath with crucial events, including the US job data set that will be released this week. Employment figures will be closely watched as they indicate upcoming rate cuts planned by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and impact the performance of Bitcoin and other major altcoins. \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials are set to speak this week, which will also give an insight into the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s position on upcoming policy plans.\par \par \uc2 US Job Data is scheduled to be published on Friday (September 6), and it will be a significant indicator of upcoming policies by the Fed and help investors understand the country\u8217\'20\'19s economic condition. Estimates have stated that the employment report is expected to show an increase of 162,000 compared to 114,000 in the previous month. The monthly unemployment rate is also expected to come down to 4.2% from the previous figure of 4.3% in July. The data is not expected to impact the upcoming rate cut plans. However, if the data throws up unexpected numbers, they could become a factor and potentially impact the broader market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Where Do BTC And Other Altcoins Go From Here?\par \par \uc2 The past week has seen the cryptocurrency markets register a substantial decline, with BTC slipping below $58,000 as the new week begins. ETH also lost the $2,500 level and is trading around the $2,450 mark. Historical data suggests BTC could dip as low as $50,000 should \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment continue in September. September has historically been a weak month for BTC, with the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency ending August 8.6% below its average of 1.75% gains, according to data from CoinGlass. CoinGlass data also supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  narrative, with BTC slipping significantly during the last week of August.\par \par \uc2 Popular trader CrypNuevo suggested there could be upside and downside liquidity hunts this week, stating,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom a trading perspective, I\u8217\'20\'19m favoring longs, so I\u8217\'20\'19d prefer seeing the move down first to hit the liquidations and fill the wick at $56.6k where I could long. So I\u8217\'20\'19m keeping a long order at that $56.6k level on Sunday & Monday in case we see a false move at the start of the week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite BTC trading in the lower half of its trading range, whales are not panicking. Instead, they continue to accumulate more BTC, using the dip as a buying opportunity. Market intelligence platform Santiment stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past month, wallets with 10-10K BTC have collectively accumulated 133.3K more coins while smaller traders continue to impatiently drop their holdings to them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another positive sign is that the amount of BTC present on major exchanges has continued to decline, with CryptoQuant data showing a 12.9% decline in crypto reserves on major exchanges since the beginning of the year. This suggests investors are \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the long term.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Markets Lost Over $300 Million In August\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency markets lost $313 million to hackers in over ten attacks executed in August. According to data from security firm PeckShield, phishing attacks accounted for 93.5% of stolen crypto, with losses totaling $293.4 million. Out of the biggest hacks in August, two phishing attacks accounted for a loss of $238 million BTC and $55 million DAI. Other major exploits in August were that of the Ronin Network. The Ronin Network managed to recover $12 million from the hacker but was the target of unauthorized crypto transactions worth $5.1 million. \uc2 DeFi\uc2  protocol Nexera also reported losses of $1.83 million due to a smart contract exploit.\par \par \uc2 First Crypto Transaction Between AI Agents\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  reported the first crypto transaction entirely managed by AI bots as the crypto industry takes a leap in developing platforms allowing AI agents to execute transactions. The transaction was overseen by Coinbase CEP \uc2 Brian Armstrong\uc2 , who announced the development on X, stating,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis week at @CoinbaseDev, we witnessed our first AI to AI crypto transaction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/08/crypto-price-analysis-8-30-btc-eth-sol-doge-xrp-dot-akt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  has gotten off to a difficult start to life in September as its price dipped to a two-week low, slipping below $58,000 late on Sunday. The dip occurred over the weekend, generally a period of low liquidity, preventing buyers from stemming the drop. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency ended August down by 8.6%, considerably lower than its monthly average gain of 1.75%, according to data from CoinGlass. With BTC entering a historically low month in the red, market watchers are worried the price could dip lower.\par \par \uc2 As we can see in the price chart, BTC has spent most of the last week of August in the red after a significant drop of 5.39% on August 27, which dragged the price below the 50 and 20-day SMAs and the $60,000 price level. The price saw considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers attempted a recovery while sellers attempted to drag the price below $58,000. In the end, BTC dropped 0.71% but stayed above $59,000, settling at $59,085. Buyers attempted another recovery on Thursday, as BTC rose to a day high of $61,230. However, with demand drying up above $60,000, sellers could push the price back below the 20-day SMA. BTC eventually settled at $59,436 after registering an increase of 0.595.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/NVZ6uFUs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC was back in the red on Friday as sellers made another attempt to drag it below the $58,000 level. Once again, buyers prevented a further drop, pushing BTC back above $59,000. BTC eventually settled at $59,163 after a decline of 0,46%. The weekend saw sellers take control and breach $58,000 on Sunday after BTC dropped 2.62% and fell to $57,399. The current session sees BTC up by 0.76% as buyers attempt to reclaim the $60,000 level. So where does BTC go from here?\par \par \uc2 After BTC dipped below $58,000 on Sunday, analysts have stated buyers must ensure it does not dip below $56,000 to maintain its long-term uptrend. One analyst stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe really need to start to bounce out of this and make a higher high to further confirm that we are in this uptrend that we\u8217\'20\'19ve been in since August. Bitcoin needs to remain above this $57.7K level; however, if it were to break down, it really, ultimately, would need to hold this $56K level; if we were to lose this $56K level, that would be a lower low.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, some analysts suggested BTC may need to drop lower before it can resume its uptrend. In fact, Markus Thielen, the head of Research at 10x Research, suggested that investors wait until BTC dips into the $40,000s to time their entry into a bull market.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 With the crypto markets entering September on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note, ETH dipped below $2,500 and retested the $2,400 support level, recording a low of $2,425. ETH has struggled to stay above the $2,600 price level despite reaching a high of $2,820 as recently as August 24. However, the price turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and by August 27, ETH dipped to $2,458 after an 8.33% decline. ETH attempted to bounce off a low of $2,402 on Wednesday, pushing above $2,500 and settling at $2,529. However, buyers lost steam on Thursday after reaching a day high of $2,597, only to drop back to $2,529.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/MH5ifhdM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Sellers dragged ETH to a low of $2,436 on Friday, but with strong demand at lower levels, the price recovered, registering only a marginal decline to remain above the crucial $2,500 level. ETH lost the $2,500 level over the weekend after a 3.44% decline on Sunday, which took the price to $2,428. However, as demand picked up close to the $2,400 support level, ETH recovered on Monday, with the price up 0.77% during the ongoing session as buyers attempted to reclaim $2,500.\par \par \uc2 August has been ETH\u8217\'20\'19s worst month since the 2020 DeFi summer. ETH\u8217\'20\'19s sharp decline in price and network fees is largely attributed to a migration to Layer2 networks and the introduction of Blobs through ERC 4337. As a result, ETH\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csound money\u8221\'20\'1D narrative has taken a hit, with its deflationary nature also not appealing to investors. The reduction in network fees has also led to a decline in rewards for ETH stakers, with fees down 90% in 2024 alone, leading to an alarmingly high inflation rate of 0.7%. As a result of these factors, ETH has struggled to break above key price levels, such as the $2,600 mark, leading to uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 For ETH to regain momentum, it must break above the $2,600 price level. A break and close above this level could see buyers target the crucial $2,850 level. However, if ETH is rejected at these levels, the prospect of a further decline could become a reality. If the $2,400 level is breached, ETH could dip to $2,300 or $2,200. With the MACD turning \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it indicates that sellers have control for now.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment around Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) intensified over the weekend as the altcoin lost the $130 level after tanking to a low of $127 on Sunday. \uc2 SOL\uc2  has struggled in recent sessions and spent last week in the red as it struggled to recapture any momentum since being rejected at $160 and dipping below $150 on Tuesday. By Friday, \uc2 SOL\uc2  had dropped to a day low of $132 as sellers threatened to overwhelm the $130 support level. However, buyers pushed the price back up to $138, with \uc2 SOL\uc2  eventually registering a decline of 1.46%. The weekend saw \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensify as \uc2 SOl\uc2  registered a 1.90% drop on Saturday to settle at $135.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/0jvTFewd/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A substantial drop of 5.03% on Sunday led to \uc2 SOL\uc2  dropping below the $130 support level, dipping to $128. Buyers attempted to reclaim $130 during the ongoing session but could not do so. \uc2 SOL\uc2  is currently down by almost 1% as sellers look to drive the price lower. Several indicators suggest that bears are in control of the market, in case the price chart and price action were not evidence enough. A downward-sloping RSI and 20-day SMA indicate strong \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment. Additionally, the MACD is also \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , indicating that sellers have control.\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2  is also witnessing declining interest from institutions, and its absence from the ETF market has also not gone unnoticed, further weighing down the price. If \uc2 SOL\uc2  continues to dip, it could slip below $120 to $116, where the price could stabilize. Buyers are expected to defend the $116 level, and a rebound could see \uc2 SOL\uc2  climb back to $130. However, if $116 breaks down, \uc2 SOL\uc2  could plunge to $100.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) is struggling to stay above $4 in the face of growing \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment after it dipped below $4.20 over the weekend. DOT, which had registered a steady uptick to $5, has now wiped out all the gains made during that uptick. After reaching a high of $5.11 last Saturday, DOT fell into the red as buyers lost steam. By Tuesday, DOT had slipped below the 20-day SMA and closed at $4.38. On Wednesday, DOT registered a decline of almost 3% as the price dipped to $4.26. With demand around the $4.20 level, sellers lost momentum as DOT registered a marginal uptick of 0.94% on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/loFmv5YP/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, buyers could not push higher as demand and liquidity dried up, allowing sellers to take control on Saturday and push DOT down by 0.70% to $4.26. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Sunday as DOT dipped below $4.20 after a drop of 4.46% to settle at $4.07. The current session sees buyers attempting a recovery, with DOT up by 1.47% and trading at $4.13. DOT is at a critical juncture, with future price movements depending on the ability of buyers to keep it above $4 and reclaim the $4.20 price level. If buyers can gain enough momentum and push DOT back to $4.20, it could lead to a push towards $4.50, where the 20-day SMA is acting as resistance. A break above this moving average could result in DOT resuming its push to $5.\par \par \uc2 On the downside, should sellers retake control of the session and push DOT below $4, it would bring its multi-year support of $3.62 into focus. We could see DOT recover with the \uc2 RSI\uc2  close to the oversold zone. However, the MACD has flipped to \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , indicating strong selling pressure.\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) is struggling to push above $6, with sellers actively defending the level, as the long wicks on August 28 suggest. Sellers are also looking to push TON below $5, with buyers struggling to keep the price afloat above the support level. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment around TON intensified as the weekend rolled in. The price dropped by 1.49% on Thursday after buyers failed to break above the 200-day SMA, falling to $5.45. TON continued to drop on Friday, registering a drop of just over 2% and settling at $5.34. After posting a recovery of 1.24% on Saturday, TON fell back into the red on Sunday, dropping by 4.30% to $5.17.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/6psKFFaW/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current session sees TON up by 0.86% and trading at $5.22. Buyers must ensure TON remains above the $5 level for any chance of a push towards $6 materializing. However, sellers will try to counter any \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum and look to breach the $5 support level. If this occurs, TON could slip to a crucial support level at $4.72.\par \par \uc2 Cosmos (ATOM) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Cosmos (ATOM) is struggling as it trades below the 20, 50, and 200-day moving averages. Since pushing to $5.34 last weekend, ATOM has been on a steady downward trajectory, dropping over 5% on August 25. By August 27, ATOM had slipped back below the 20-day SMA, following a drop of almost 6%, and settled at $4.60. Wednesday and Thursday saw increased \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers and sellers struggled to establish dominance, with ATOM registering only marginal increases on both days. Sellers attempted to drive the price below $4 on Friday, but with demand picking up at lower levels, buyers could counteract and push the price up by 0.90% to $4.65.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/5SoJdrPi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned over the weekend as ATOM dropped by 1.92% on Saturday and 5.62% on Sunday to end the week at $4.30. The current session sees ATOM up by 0.87% as buyers look to move back to $4.50. Until last week, buyers sought to breach the $5 price level. However, recent \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment has left ATOM close to its $ support level. For any upward momentum to take hold, buyers must push ATOM above the 20-day SMA, currently around the $4.70 mark. A break above this level could lead to a move towards $5.\par \par \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) is currently among the worst-performing meme coins, with the price down a staggering 24% over the past month. In fact, data from Lookonchain shows WIF is down almost 71% from its 52-week high. Things are going from bad to worse for the Solana-based meme coin, with its price turning \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  after failing to breach the $2 price level on August 24. As a result, WIF began the previous week in the red and by Tuesday (August 27) dipped below the 20-day SMA after a drop of almost 11%, which dragged the price to $1.57. Sellers attempted to pull the price lower on Wednesday but were thwarted as buyers began their own attempt to move above the 20-day SMA. In the end WIF could only register a marginal increase and remained below the SMA.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/voY0i3Aa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Sellers thwarted another attempt to move above the 20-day SMA on Thursday, pushing WIF down from a day high of $1.69. Sellers eventually drove the price down almost 3% to $1.53 and attempted to push it lower on Friday, with the price dropping to a low of $1.43 before climbing back up to $1.54. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment took over during the weekend as WIF dropped 1.68% on Saturday and over 8% on Sunday to settle just below $1.40. The current session sees WIF up by 1.33% as buyers attempt to push back above the $1.40 support level.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240903ek9200003\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , XRP, DOGE, TON,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s bounce off $57,000 is encouraging but a decisive close above $60,000 is really needed to begin the path back toward the range-highs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWIzOTMtNjM5NS03MTlkLTk2NGYtNTAxMzI1YjdjMWU4.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index (SPX) rose marginally by 0.24% last week, but Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) succumbed to selling pressure and fell nearly 11%. Will Bitcoin resume its uptrend, or has it already topped out? That is the big question worrying investors.\par \par \uc2 However, the whales do not seem to be perturbed by the sideways price action and have been on a buying spree. According to a post on X by market intelligence platform Santiment, Bitcoin whale wallets holding 100 Bitcoin or more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-whale-wallets-hit-17-month-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged by 283 wallets to 16,129 wallets}}}\uc2 , the highest in 17 months.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b388-f6f0-7a46-8140-7b320e4b38a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin could be under pressure in the near term as September has historically been a weak month for Bitcoin, with an average return of -4.45%. However, market participants are looking further out, expecting a strong performance in October, which has an average return of 22.90%, according to CoinGlass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coinglass.com/today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin stay above $55,724, extending its sideways price action? Will that attract buying in altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index has been consolidating in a tight range just below the all-time high of 5,670, indicating that the bulls are in no hurry to book profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b389-9d05-7603-8cd1-35d8dd883704"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day exponential moving average (5,544) and the relative strength index (RSI) in the positive territory indicate the possibility of an upside breakout. If that happens, the index may start the next leg of the uptrend toward 6,000.\par \par \uc2 If bears want to prevent the upside, they will have to drag the price back below the moving averages. If they do that, the selling may pick up, and the index could decline toward 5,265. That may keep the index range-bound between 5,119 and 5,670 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 US Dollar Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The US Dollar Index (DXY) rebounded sharply off 100.50, indicating solid demand from the bulls at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38a-5411-7ffc-b845-f9efcdf42c9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The relief rally is expected to face stiff resistance at the 20-day EMA (102). If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears will again attempt to sink the index below 100.50. If they do that, the next stop may be 99.57.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if buyers drive the price above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the selling pressure is reducing. The index may then attempt a rally to the 50-day simple moving average (103).\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin closed below the immediate support of $58,000 on Sept. 1, but the bears failed to drag the price to the pivotal level of $55,724. This suggests demand at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38b-0072-77f7-a3a7-f875e3d9c521"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to push the price above the moving averages. If they can pull it off, the BTC/USDT pair may rally to $65,000. This level is expected to act as a formidable hurdle in the near term. That will keep the pair inside the large range between $55,724 and $73,777 for some more days.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA ($60,007), the bears will make one more attempt to yank the price below $55,724. If they are successful, the pair could plunge to the Aug. 5 intraday low of $49,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the immediate support at $2,392 on Sept. 2, indicating that the bulls are trying to form a higher low.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38b-e7d5-7775-aa8d-ecccea13159f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The relief rally is expected to face selling at the 20-day EMA ($2,605). If the price turns down sharply from the 20-day EMA, the bears will attempt to sink the ETH/USDT pair to $2,300 and then to $2,111.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day EMA. That will clear the path for a possible rise to the breakdown level of $2,850. Buyers will have to overcome this barrier to suggest that the downtrend may be over.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside the large range between $460 and $635 for the past several weeks, indicating buying on dips and selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38c-9de9-704c-bf52-ba9a934e4e8f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The BNB/USDT pair turned down from the moving averages on Sept. 1 but bounced off the $495 support on Sept. 2. This suggests that the buyers will fiercely defend the $460 to $495 support zone.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the moving averages are the important resistance levels that need to be crossed to attract buyers. A close above the 50-day SMA ($549) could push the pair to $600 and subsequently to $635.\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) broke below the $129 support on Sept. 1, but the bulls purchased the dip and pushed the price back above the level on Sept. 2.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38d-513a-76c2-81cf-8e05b0974ad5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains above $129, the bulls will try to push the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair above the 20-day EMA ($143). If they do that, the pair could rally to the overhead resistance of $164. This level may act as a significant hurdle in the short term.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative. That may sink the pair to the critical support at $116. Buyers will try to defend this level with all their might because a break below it could open the gates for a fall to $100.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($0.57) on Aug. 31 and reached the solid support at $0.54 on Sept. 1.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38e-0be1-72d2-aa65-955090951a4c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 A break and close below $0.54 will open the doors for a fall to $0.49. The XRP/USDT pair may then oscillate inside the $0.41 to $0.64 range for some more time.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the moving averages, it will suggest that the bulls continue to buy on dips. The pair may then climb to the stiff overhead resistance of $0.64. Buyers will have to overcome this barrier to start the next leg of the up move to $0.74.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/is-solana-price-dropping-under-100-in-september"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Is Solana price dropping under $100 in September?}}}\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($0.10) on Sept. 1, indicating that the bears continue to sell on minor rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38e-cfe5-792f-9fc8-9d266a36e1c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 Minor support is at $0.09, but if the bulls fail to defend the level, the selling could intensify, and the DOGE/USDT pair may plunge to $0.08 and eventually to the support line of the falling wedge pattern.\par \par \uc2 The bulls have an uphill task in front of them. If they want to signal a potential trend change, buyers will have to push and sustain the pair above the downtrend line. The pair may then start a new up move to $0.14.\par \par \uc2 Toncoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/toncoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TON}}}\uc2  ) has been forming a large \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head-and-shoulders pattern, which will complete on a break and close below $4.72.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b38f-82e2-7033-960f-34a87a4e40f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 TON/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  in the negative territory indicate that bears are in control. There is minor support at $5.12, but that is likely to be broken. The TON/USDT pair may fall to $4.72, which is expected to witness aggressive buying by the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the price bounces off $4.72 and breaks above the 20-day EMA ($5.81), it will suggest that the selling pressure is reducing. The pair may then climb to the 50-day SMA ($6.38). Such a move will suggest that the pair may extend its stay inside the $4.72 to $8.29 range for a while.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) slipped below the uptrend line on Sept. 1, but the bears are struggling to sustain the lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b390-61ca-78e0-893a-413bc96dfc42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price maintains above the uptrend line, the bulls will again try to propel the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair above the moving averages. If they succeed, the pair may reach the downtrend line. Buyers will have to kick and sustain the price above the downtrend line to signal a short-term trend change.\par \par \uc2 If the price fails to remain above the uptrend line, the slide could reach $0.31. This level is likely to witness strong buying by the bulls, but if the bears prevail, the pair may drop to $0.27 and later to the crucial support of $0.24.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDkvMDE5MWIzOTMtNjM5NS03MTlkLTk2NGYtNTAxMzI1YjdjMWU4.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240902ek92000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Market\par \b \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Cointelegraph \par \uc2 600 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Need to know what happened in crypto today? Here is the latest news on daily trends and events impacting Bitcoin price, blockchain, DeFi, NFTs, Web3 and crypto \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNzhkNzg3NjEtM2JkMi00NTY5LTk2YTctNjJhOTdmMGExYjBh.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today}}}\par \par \uc2 Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court has upheld a judge\u8217\'20\'19s recent decision to suspend the X social media platform in the country, and cryptocurrency investment products witnessed major outflows of $305 million in the last week of August. Meanwhile, layer-1 blockchain Cardano has upgraded via its long-awaited Chang hard fork, bringing in a shift to decentralized governance.\par \par \uc2 Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court upholds X suspension\par \par \uc2 A Brazilian Supreme Court panel has upheld a recent decision to suspend access to X in the country.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/brazil-supreme-court-judge-suspend-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a unanimous decision}}}\uc2 , five Supreme Court Justices supported Justice \uc2 Alexandre de Moraes\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Aug. 30 ruling to suspend the social media platform. Moraes\u8217\'20\'19 decision was handed down after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/brazil-supreme-court-bans-twitter-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X CEO Elon Musk refused}}}\uc2  to name a legal representative for the company\u8217\'20\'19s Brazilian operations.\par \par \uc2 According to an Associated Press report, Moraes followed through with his intention to suspend the platform after X\u8217\'20\'19s Global Government Affairs team said it \u8220\'20\'1Cwould not comply with [de Moraes\u8217\'20\'19] illegal orders to censor political opponents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Musk has doubled down on his criticism of Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s justice system, calling Moraes \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator.\u8221\'20\'1D Musk has also said that VPN usage would likely surge as more Brazilians sought to bypass the suspension. However, Brazilians caught using a VPN to access X could face fines of up to 50,000 reais, or $8,900.\par \par \uc2 According to Moraes, X will remain suspended until the company pays outstanding fines of more than $3 million.\par \par \uc2 Crypto products hit with $305M outflow amid strong US economic data\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency investment products witnessed major outflows of $305 million last week amid strong economic reports in the United States.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-09/0191b26f-ec82-79bf-9d40-ab39ca34ba2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto investment flows by country, Aug. 24\u8211\'20\'13Aug. 31. Source: \uc2 CoinShares\par \par \uc2 Germany and Sweden posted smaller outflows totaling $7.3 million and $4.3 million, respectively. On the other hand, Switzerland and Canada saw slight inflows totaling $5.5 million and $13.2 million, respectively.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to expect the asset class to become increasingly sensitive to interest rate expectations as the Fed gets closer to a pivot,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  noted in its latest report.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Commerce Department\uc2  reported on Aug. 30 that the Personal Consumption Expenditures (PCE) price index surged 0.2% on the month and was also up 2.5% from the same period last year.\par \par \uc2 Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s Chang hard fork goes live as it shifts to decentralized governance\par \par \uc2 The Cardano blockchain has successfully undergone its highly anticipated hard fork, upgrading voting mechanisms and smart contracts and heralding a new era of decentralized governance.\par \par \uc2 On Sept. 1, at 21:44 UTC at block 10764778, the layer-1 proof-of-stake blockchain underwent the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-the-cardano-chang-hard-fork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chang upgrade}}}\uc2 , which ushered in what the project calls the \u8220\'20\'1CConway ledger era.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One small step for Cardano; One giant leap for the industry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ENXV41XdhZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ENXV41XdhZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Charles Hoskinson\uc2  (@IOHK_Charles) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IOHK_Charles/status/1830292210706948531?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 One of the key changes is transforming Cardano governance enabling any \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) holder to submit or participate in the voting process for governance actions as part of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-voltaire-era-june-hard-fork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 project\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CVoltaire\u8221\'20\'1D upgrade phase}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a post on X on Sept. 2, the Cardano Foundation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Cardano_CF/status/1830411972460093781"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s Chang hard fork marks a major milestone for the Cardano blockchain, ecosystem, and community\u8211\'20\'13\u8211\'20\'13fulfilling the promise of a truly self-governing, decentralized network.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNzhkNzg3NjEtM2JkMi00NTY5LTk2YTctNjJhOTdmMGExYjBh.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\