\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 8-28 BTC, ETH, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOGE, TAO, FET, MATIC\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,561 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC), Ethereum (ETH) Register Sharp Drops}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC And ETH Lead Liquidations}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trends Suggest Difficult September For BTC}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bittensor (TAO) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FET Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polygon (MATIC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Major cryptocurrencies, including Bitcoin (BTC) and Ethereum (ETH), saw a significant drop as $170 million in long positions were liquidated in one hour, according to data from CoinGlass. This hurt investors who had bet on the prices of both cryptocurrencies to rise further.\par \par \uc2 The liquidations were dominated by BTC and ETH investors, with $65 million and $52 million in long positions liquidated, respectively. BTC plummeted below $60,000 late on Tuesday and has dipped by 6% in the past 24 hours. Meanwhile, ETH crashed below the crucial $2,500 level, down over 8% in the past 24 hours. Other cryptocurrencies, including Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Dogecoin (DOGE), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Toncoin (TON), and Polkadot (DOT) also registered notable drops.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC), Ethereum (ETH) Register Sharp Drops\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) pushed above $63,000 on Friday following reports that Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  was preparing for an interest rate cut next month, pulling the price of other altcoins higher as well. However, the price dropped sharply following the liquidations, dampening the market\u8217\'20\'19s mood. The traditional stock markets mainly traded flat for the day, with analysts not finding any specific trigger for the drop.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts pointed to the recent state of Bitcoin price movements achieving equilibrium, with one report from CoinGlass noting that it might precede a period of heightened \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Meanwhile, Fairland Strategies suggested that BTC could be in for a difficult September, pointing to several factors indicating potential weakness. Fairland Strategies stated in its report,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are entering a seasonally weak period in September for risk assets broadly. A correction usually impacts the most volatile assets the hardest, albeit temporarily. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are now minor signs of upside exhaustion per the DeMARK Indicators, and once the daily stochastics turn below 80%, it would increase the risk that support (~$56,500) is retested.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BTC And ETH Lead Liquidations\par \par \uc2 The crypto markets witnessed over $313 million in liquidations on Tuesday as BTC dipped below $60,000. Long traders bore the brunt of these liquidations, sustaining 90%, worth $282 million. This is significantly more than the $31 million in short liquidations. Ethereum(ETH) liquidations were the highest, with over $100 million, of which $93.5 million were liquidated in long positions. As a result, ETH dipped below the crucial $2,500 price level and still hasn\u8217\'20\'19t recovered. BTC was a close second with over $94 million in liquidations, with its open interest also registering a considerable drop. Open interest refers to the number of unsettled long and short positions in the market, with a drop suggesting increased liquidations or a cautionary approach from traders.\par \par \uc2 Trends Suggest Difficult September For BTC\par \par \uc2 With Bitcoin (BTC) witnessing a drop towards the end of October, market watchers are hoping for better prospects in September. However, historical data suggests that September has not been kind to the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency. BTC has ended September in the red eight times in the past 11 years and struggled even during highly \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  years such as 2013, 2017, and 2021. However, BTC could break the trend this year, with the US election as a potential catalyst.\par \par \uc2 Many have predicted that the US election results could significantly impact the price of BTC. Another catalyst for a potential increase is the possibility of a rate cut in September, as hinted by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  during the Federal Open Market Committee meeting. Looking ahead, October has been a traditionally strong month for BTC, with prices registering an increase in nine out of the past eleven years.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/08/crypto-price-analysis-8-27-btc-eth-sol-wif-dot-tia-avax-ton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  saw a wave of liquidations late on Tuesday, leading to a substantial drop in price. This hurt traders who had bet on the asset\u8217\'20\'19s price to increase following the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement of a rate cut in September. However, the liquidations have dampened the optimism around BTC, which has dropped over 6% over the past 24 hours. As a result, the price has dipped below the crucial $60,000 price level once again, with buyers struggling to establish a foothold.\par \par \uc2 As we can see in the price chart below, BTC had been in an upward trajectory as the previous week drew to a close, rising by 3.50% on Wednesday before a slight drop on Thursday as the 50-day SMA came into play, allowing sellers to push BTC down by just over 1%. However, bulls took control on Friday, with BTC registering an increase of 5.97%, pushing above the 50- and 200-day SMAs to settle at $64,032. In fact, BTC reached a day high of $65,054, but sellers pushed the price back below $65,000, a level they were expected to defend vigorously.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/RTQuC2hg/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The weekend saw buyers and sellers struggle to take control, with BTC only managing a marginal increase on Saturday. Sunday saw buyers attempt another push towards $65,000 while sellers tried to drive the price below the 200-day SMA. However, neither could establish control, and BTC remained at $64,085. The current week began with BTC dipping below the 200-day SMA after a 1.85% drop as sellers tightened their grip on the market. As a result, BTC dropped to $62,903. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Tuesday as markets crashed, with BTC dropping by 5.40% to slip below the 50 and 20-day SMAs and the $60,000 price level to $59,506. The current session sees BTC remain in the red, down by 0.50%, as sellers look to drive the price lower.\par \par \uc2 With Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s reversal, sellers have established control in the market, with any move above $64,000 ruled out for the time being. With September historically being a difficult month for BTC, it could drop further should sellers remain in control. Buyers will attempt to regroup and reclaim the $60,000 level, which is crucial to resume a push back above the moving averages and move towards $64,000. Should sellers continue to dominate, BTC could drop to the $58,000 support level.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 With the crypto markets experiencing a significant drop last night, Ethereum (ETH) tumbled below the crucial $2,500 level, dashing hopes of a push toward the $2,850 support level. The overall crypto market has registered a drop of almost 8% since the week began, with major cryptocurrencies spending a third consecutive day in the red. ETH recorded almost $100 million in liquidations, resulting in an almost 9% drop in the past 24 hours, wiping out the gains made on Friday.\par \par \uc2 ETH had jumped by 5.36% after pushing above the 20-day SMA as buyers successfully broke above the $2,700 price level despite strong selling pressure. Sellers attempted to regain control on Saturday, pushing ETH down from its day high of $2,820. However, buyers prevented a drop below $2,700, with ETH instead registering a marginal increase to end the day at $2,769. Sellers took control of the market on Sunday, pushing ETH down by 0.75% to $2,749.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/hGuJw9yX/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Monday as ETH lost the $2,700 level after a drop of 2.42% and fell to $2,682. The late-night crash on Tuesday took ETH below the 20-day SMA and the crucial $2,500 support level as the price crashed over 8% to $2,458. Sellers pushed ETH to a low of $2,397 before buyers clawed back to $2,458. The current session sees ETH marginally down as sellers attempt to drive the price lower while buyers look to reclaim the $2,500 level. ETH\u8217\'20\'19s price has struggled to recover since the August 5 market crash and now stands at a crucial juncture.\par \par \uc2 If sellers retain control and push ETH lower, it could drop to the $2,200 support level. Buyers must reclaim the $2,500 level for a recovery to occur and prevent further decline.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) mirrored the markets, spending the week in the red and dipping below $150 and the moving averages. \uc2 SOL\uc2  entered the weekend on a highly positive note, surging over 7% on Friday, pushing above the 20 and 200-day SMAs, and reclaiming the crucial $150 price level to settle at $153. \uc2 SOL\uc2  continued to push higher on Saturday as well, rising by almost 5% to go above $160 and settling at $160.78. However, sellers lost steam on Sunday, as sellers took control and drove \uc2 SOL\uc2  back below $160 to settle at $159.10.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/YMVlQ7S2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers attempted a recovery on Monday, as \uc2 SOL\uc2  rose to a day high of $162. Despite starting strongly, \uc2 SOL\uc2  lost steam at higher levels as sellers took control and pushed the price down by 1.18% to $157.22. The price remained \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, dropping below $150 and the moving averages after a 6.55% drop and settling at $146.92. The current session sees \uc2 SOL\uc2  remain in the red, down by 1.35% and trading around the $144 mark. So, where does \uc2 SOL\uc2  go from here? Sellers will look to drive the price below $140. Should this happen, it would indicate that sellers have established control in the market. On their part, buyers will look to defend the lower levels and reclaim $150 to resume the push to $160.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) slumped with the rest of the markets, wiping out the gains made during the previous week, as bears drove the price below the $0.100 support level. DOGE lost momentum after hitting $0.112 on Friday after an increase of 6.52%. However, the price was rejected at the 50-day SMA, leading to a marginal drop on Saturday. DOGE also remained \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday, registering a drop of 2.41% to settle at $0.109. The current week began with \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensifying, with DOGE dropping by almost 4% to $0.105.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/KIWpsOyL/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The late-night crash on Tuesday dragged DOGE lower as it lost the $0.100 support level, dropping to $0.098 after a nearly 6% decline. The current session sees DOGE marginally up as buyers attempt to reclaim the $0.100 support level. If they are successful, DOGE will look for an initial push up to $0.105, where the 20-day SMA could act as resistance. A break above this level will see buyers attempt to reclaim $0.110. However, should sentiment remain \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , DOGE could drop to $0.095 or even as low as $0.090.\par \par \uc2 Bittensor (TAO) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 AI-related tokens have been on an upward trajectory, with investors turning to them in anticipation of \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s earnings report, which is set to be released this week. One such token is TAO, which had been quite \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the weekend. In fact, TAO registered significant jumps of 7.89% on Thursday and 8.08% on Friday to surge towards $350. With sellers active at this level, TAO dropped on Saturday, falling by just over 2% to $338. However, it quickly recovered, registering a jump of 3.13% on Sunday despite strong selling pressure and considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as sellers attempted to lower the price.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/mSyBi3oR/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current week began with TAO in the red, dropping by 3.34% to $337. Buyers attempted a move above $350 on Tuesday, with TAO reaching a day high of $364. However, with the broader crypto markets witnessing a decline, TAO fell in the red, and sellers yanked the price down by 7.23% to $313. TAO hit a low of $303 before rebounding from the moving averages to settle at $313. The current session sees buyers and sellers vying for control. Sellers attempted to push TAO below the moving averages and $300, but with strong demand at lower levels, TAO could recover and climb to its current level of $312. If buyers can retain control, we could see the price push back towards $350.\par \par \uc2 FET Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 FET has registered an incredible 40% increase over the past 7 days, surging above $1 to hit $1.35 on Sunday. However, its momentum has waned this week, with sellers dragging the price down since Monday and buyers struggling to establish a foothold during the ongoing session. FET has been \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  since August 19 and registered an incredible 18.73% increase on Friday to push above the 50-day SMA and settle at $1.20. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment prevailed over the weekend as well, with FET registering a 4.98% increase on Saturday and an even more significant increase of 7.74% on Sunday to settle at $1.36.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/OifuuL6H/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, FET also faced considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday as sellers attempted to push the price down to $1.10, an attempt buyers could thwart. Despite ending the weekend on a hugely positive note, FET fell into the red on Monday, dropping by 2.12% to $1.33. Buyers attempted a recovery on Tuesday, pushing FET to a day high of $1.47, but lost momentum, allowing sellers to drag the price back down. As a result, FET dropped by 3.59% to $1.28, with sellers firmly in control. The current session sees buyers and sellers vying for control. FET dropped to a day low of $1.18 but has since recovered thanks to lower-level demand and is currently trading at $1.28.\par \par \uc2 If sellers retain control of the ongoing session, they will attempt to drive FET towards $1.10. However, buyers are expected to defend this level, and the price could rebound from the 50-day SMA. If buyers regain control, we could see FET attempt another move towards $1.50.\par \par \uc2 Polygon (MATIC) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Polygon (MATIC) has plummeted almost 12% over the past 24 hours after losing a crucial support level and dropping below the 20 and 50-day SMAs. MATIC, which had been quite \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the previous week, pushed above the $0.55 resistance level on Saturday, rising to $0.57 after a 6.12% increase. However, buyers lost steam as selling pressure intensified at upper levels. As a result, the price dropped over 8% on Sunday, slipping back below $0.55 and settling at $0.52.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/KjJhLHrC/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC remained in the red on Monday as well, starting the week on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note after dropping by 4.19% and settling at $0.50. With the crypto markets crashing late on Tuesday, MATIC dropped over 7% on Wednesday, slipping below the 50-day SMA and a crucial support level and settling at $0.46. The current session sees the price down by 3.43% and below the 20-day SMA. If MATIC remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we could see sellers drive the price down to $0.40, a support level buyers are expected to defend. A rebound from this level could start a relief rally, leading to a climb back to $0.50.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240829ek8s00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , XRP, DOGE, TON,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 AVAX\uc2 , SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,698 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s fall below $60,000 has pulled several altcoins lower, but a rebound could be in the making.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvMDE5MTk5ZGUtNTA1Mi03ODhiLWFlNTItYmJhNDdmMTI2Mzlk.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) continues to witness random and volatile price action inside the $55,724 to $73,777 range. Although it is difficult to predict the direction of the breakout from the range, long-term investors remain \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . CryptoQuant data shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-exchanges-third-biggest-net-daily-outflow-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 net outflows of roughly 45,000 Bitcoin from exchanges}}}\uc2  on Aug. 27, the third highest outflows.\par \par \uc2 In addition to Bitcoin, investors seem keen on accumulating Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) though the price action has been subdued. Popular analyst Satoshi Sniper highlighted in his post on X that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ether-whales-accumulate-540m-price-bottom-nears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ether whales had added 200,000 Ether}}}\uc2  worth roughly $540 million in the past four days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199cb-1153-78c1-b425-7fd54e48a901"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 However, Bloomberg Intelligence senior commodity strategist \uc2 Mike McGlone\uc2  suggested in his latest analysis on X that the risk-asset race \u8220\'20\'1Cmay be over.\u8221\'20\'1D According to McGlone, Bitcoin peaked at 15 times the value of the S&P 500 (SPX) in the first quarter of 2020, and the high in 2024 was 14 times. He projects a possible {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-11x-sp-500-bitcoin-rolling-over-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50% drop toward 7 times}}}\uc2  the value of the S&P 500.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin plummet to $55,724, or will it climb to $65,000? How are the altcoins likely to behave? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s failure to break above $65,000 on Aug. 25 suggests that demand dries up at higher levels. That started a pullback, which dropped below the moving averages on Aug. 27.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199cb-cc1f-76d7-b0f3-292e0b394ee9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are trying to form a higher low at $58,000, but the relief rally is likely to face selling at the moving averages. If the price continues lower or turns down from the 20-day exponential moving average ($60,9046), it will suggest that bears remain in charge. The BTC/USDT pair may then slump to $55,724.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are the near-term resistance levels to watch out for. If buyers overcome this hurdle, the pair may retest the $65,000 resistance. A break and close above this level will signal that the advantage has tilted in favor of the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether turned down from the breakdown level of $2,850 on Aug. 24, indicating that the bears have flipped the level into resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199cc-98ad-7f21-aa73-f89db35d77e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling picked up after the ETH/USDT pair closed below the 20-day EMA ($2,670) on Aug. 26. The bears will try to pull the price to the solid support at $2,300. This is an important level to watch out for because a break below it may result in a retest of the Aug. 5 intraday low of $2,111.\par \par \uc2 If the price rises from the current level or rebounds off $2,300, it will signal demand at lower levels. That may keep the pair stuck inside the $2,300 to $2,850 range for a few days.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside a large range between $460 and $635 for several months, indicating buying on dips and selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199cd-4f54-7248-8b02-9e4101243572"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages have flattened out, and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  is just below the midpoint, indicating that the range-bound action may continue for some more time. If the price remains below the moving averages, the bears will try to sink the BNB/USDT pair to the $495 to $460 support zone.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if buyers push the price above the moving averages, the likelihood of a rally to $600 and thereafter to $635 increases. The next trending move will begin on a break above $635 or below $460.\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) turned down and plunged below the moving averages on Aug. 27, indicating that higher levels are attracting sellers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199ce-01ff-7a25-a8f8-f15764f495f9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to stall the down move in the $129 to $136 support zone. If the price bounces off the support zone, it is likely to face selling at the moving averages. If the price turns down and breaks below $129, the next stop is expected to be $116. Buyers will try to vigorously defend this level.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to gain the upper hand, they will have to push and maintain the price above $164. The \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair may then climb to $189.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been trading between $0.64 and $0.54 for the past few days, indicating that the bulls are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199ce-b8c4-760e-be34-3adf122a5df2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to push the price above the moving averages. If they do that, the XRP/USDT pair may climb to the $0.64 overhead resistance. This is a formidable hurdle to cross, but if the bulls prevail, the pair may rally to $0.74.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA ($0.58), the bears will make another effort to sink the pair below $0.54. If they succeed, the pair could start a decline toward $0.46.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) reversed direction from the 50-day SMA ($0.11) on Aug. 24 and broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.10) on Aug. 26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199cf-8332-7b3c-9f73-6dbe16a2000e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOGE/USDT pair will try to find support in the $0.10 to $0.09 zone. Buyers will have to push and retain the price above the falling wedge to suggest that the downtrend could be over. The pair may then attempt a rally to $0.14.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price plunges below the support zone, it will suggest that the bears remain in control. The pair may decline to the strong support at $0.08 and thereafter to the support line.\par \par \uc2 Toncoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/toncoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TON}}}\uc2  ) turned down sharply from the 50-day SMA ($6.58) on Aug. 24 and broke below the $5.26 support on Aug. 26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199d0-392a-71c6-8d55-34dc023e2825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 TON/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages have started to turn down, and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  is in the negative territory, indicating that the bears have the edge. The TON/USDT pair is likely to drop to the crucial support at $4.72. Buyers will try to defend this level with all their might because if the support breaks, the pair will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head-and-shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated in the short term if the price continues higher and breaks above the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-green-monthly-close-64-3k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can Bitcoin get a green monthly close above $64.3K?}}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) turned down and slipped below the 50-day SMA ($0.38) on Aug. 26, signaling that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199d1-2c9b-708d-9261-54508b741b8a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair continued lower and broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.36) on Aug. 27. Minor support at the uptrend line, but if that breaks down, the pair may slide to $0.31.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns up from the current level or the uptrend line, the bulls will again try to drive the pair above the 50-day SMA. If they do that, the likelihood of a rally to the downtrend line increases. Buyers will have to clear this hurdle to signal a potential trend change in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Avalanche price analysis\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the resistance line of the descending channel pattern on Aug. 25, indicating that the bears are aggressively defending the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199d1-e828-723b-aa8f-262b1e71f930"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price has reached the 20-day EMA ($23.89), an essential level for the bulls to defend. If the price rebounds off the current level with strength, it will suggest buying on dips. That will improve the prospects of a rally above the channel. The AVAX/USDT pair may then climb to $33 and later to $37.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the pair may fall to $19.50, extending its stay inside the channel for some more time.\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu price analysis\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to sustain Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) above the 50-day SMA ($0.000015) attracted selling by short-term traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/019199d2-9433-789d-9e58-8d86025ca2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, DOGE, TON, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 The SHIB/USDT pair turned down from the 50-day SMA on Aug. 25 and broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.000014) on Aug. 27. Buyers are trying to take support at the uptrend line, but if the bears prevail, the pair may drop to $0.000012. This level is again expected to act as a strong support.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to push and maintain the price above $0.000016 to signal the start of a sustained recovery toward $0.000020.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvMDE5MTk5ZGUtNTA1Mi03ODhiLWFlNTItYmJhNDdmMTI2Mzlk.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240828ek8s000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
