\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 8-14 BTC, ETH, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , TON, SHIB, UNI, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,436 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Markets Register Growth}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spot Bitcoin And Ethereum ETFs See Turnaround}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toncoin (TON) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shiba Inu (SHIB) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Global crypto markets registered a 104% year-on-year (YoY) increase in market cap, with Bitcoin (BTC) remaining a standout performer, with growth of between 50% and 55%.\par \par \uc2 Several factors contributed to BTC and the crypto market\u8217\'20\'19s performance during the current year. Chief among these factors were the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) \u8217\'20\'19s approval of spot Bitcoin and Ethereum ETFs, the fourth Bitcoin halving, and the launch of Runes.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the co-founder of Bitmex, \uc2 Arthur Hayes\uc2 , has predicted BTC will hit $100k by the end of the year and a staggering $1 million by the end of 2025, outlining several factors that could drive a surge in BTC and the broader financial market.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Markets Register Growth\par \par \uc2 A report by Binance revealed that the market capitalization of virtual digital assets registered a growth of $720 billion during the calendar year. This is a 44% increase year-to-date and a 104% increase year-on-year (Y0Y). The report also sheds light on how growth in the crypto market has outpaced the traditional markets. Major stock indices such as Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s Hang Seng Index and UK\u8217\'20\'19s FTSE 100 have registered only single-digit growth in the year\u8217\'20\'19s first half. In comparison, major cryptocurrencies such as BTC and Ethereum (ETH) have outperformed the markets by a wide margin. According to Binance CEO Richard Teng, the first half of 2024 has been remarkable for the crypto markets.\par \par \uc2 BTC\u8217\'20\'19s dominance has been unrivaled thanks to the launch of spot Bitcoin ETFs, the halving event, and the launch of Runes. US spot ETFs have attracted inflows of over $17 billion and an average daily trading volume of $2.5 billion. Teng stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first half of 2024 has been remarkable for the global VDA market. Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s increased market dominance and the enthusiastic reception of both Bitcoin and Ether ETFs highlight the growing appeal of VDAs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Spot Bitcoin And Ethereum ETFs See Turnaround\par \par \uc2 US-based spot Bitcoin and Ethereum ETFs started the week on a positive note. Spot Bitcoin ETFs registered inflows worth almost $28 million on Monday, while spot Ethereum ETFs saw inflows worth nearly $5 million, marking a departure from the recent trend of significant outflows. However, in the case of Ethereum, this is a modest amount given the $401 million worth of outflows witnessed since July.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum is attracting considerable interest after the market correction, with investors pouring in significant capital, over $150 million, marking a resurgence for the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest cryptocurrency. While ETH saw a significant \b \highlight22\uc2 price drop\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors saw a strategic buying opportunity. With the capital inflow, ETH\u8217\'20\'19s net inflows have crossed a total of $850 million since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 Besides Ethereum, several other major cryptocurrencies have also registered a sharp rebound. BTC also registered considerable interest, although its net inflows of $13 million were dwarfed by ETH. Despite being modest, the turnaround marks a renewed interest in BTC and other crypto assets. Short positions on BTC also registered a notable decline, signaling that investors were not betting on an extended decline. Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Ripple (XRP), and Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) also registered notable inflows of $4.5 million, $0.7 million, and $0.6 million, respectively, further fueling the idea that the recent correction could be ending.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/08/crypto-price-analysis-8-13-btc-eth-sol-ada-bch-doge-and-mkr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  was able to reverse its recent price woes and break above $60,000 as buyers returned to the market in droves. Crossing the psychologically important $60,000 price level could mark a turnaround in the fortunes of BTC and possibly allow it to break above the moving averages as it looks to regain lost ground after a decline that yanked it from highs of $70,000 to below $50,000 at one point. Markets also seem to have turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Bitmex co-founder predicting BTC could hit $100,000 by the end of 2024 and a staggering $1 million by the end of 2025.\par \par \uc2 Another report from \uc2 Bitfinex\uc2  analyzed BTC\u8217\'20\'19s rebound and potential local bottom. BTC has surged almost 30% since hitting a recent low of $49,000 to push above $60,000 this week. The \uc2 Bitfinex\uc2  report examined BTC\u8217\'20\'19s recovery through various metrics and gave key insights into whether or not BTC was approaching a local bottom. Looking at the BTC price chart, we can see that BTC lost momentum after Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s 12% surge as the moving averages came into play. As a result, BTC turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, dropping by 1.34%. The price continued its \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trajectory as well and dropped by almost 4% on Sunday to slip below $60,000 and settle at $58,775.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/l70WIfef/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the sentiment changed as the new week rolled in, as bears mounted a strong push to take BTC above $60,000, reaching an intra-day high of $60,750. However, strong selling pressure pushed BTC back down, eventually settling at $59,410. BTC finally broke above $60,000 on Tuesday after an increase of 2.10% took it to $60,658. Buyers also attempted a move above the moving averages but were thwarted. The current session sees BTC trading at $60,842, marginally up compared to Tuesday. It\u8217\'20\'19s clear from the price chart that BTC faces considerable resistance at the moving averages, with the 50 and 200-day SMAs also performing a death cross.\par \par \uc2 Buyers are attempting to surpass this level but have so far been unsuccessful. However, if they can consolidate above $60,000, we could see BTC retest these levels again. A break above these levels could see BTC push towards $65,000. Sellers will try to drive BTC back below $60,000; if successful, we could see the \b \highlight22\uc2 price drop\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards $58,000.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) has been positive this week, having registered an increase of 2.30% over the past 24 hours and over 9% during the past week. If we look at ETH\u8217\'20\'19s recent low of $2,100, the price has rallied by around 27%. However, ETH has struggled to move above $2,800 despite this and is consolidating under $3,000. As we can see from the price chart, ETH has witnessed considerable price movement since the August 5 crash. A sharp recovery on Thursday pushed ETH to $2,684. However, buyers lost momentum, and ETH was back in the red on Friday. By Sunday, ETH had dropped down to $2,556 after a 2.09% drop on the day.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/aK8Qaciz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH made a strong start to the current week, registering an increase of 6.52% on Monday to push above $2,700 and settle at $2,723. However, the price fell back on Tuesday as sellers attempted to drive the price below $2,500. However, demand at lower levels prevented that, allowing ETH to recover. The price eventually settled at $2,703 after a drop of 0.71%. The current session sees ETH marginally up and trading at $2,724. ETH is evidently struggling to push above the $2,700-$2,800 zone, with buyers repeatedly losing momentum at these levels. So, what happens to the ETH price from here?\par \par \uc2 ETH is encountering considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Bollinger bands highlighting increased \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If buyers push ETH above the $2,700-$2,800 level, we could see a move towards $3,000. A break above this level could see a move to the Bollinger bands\u8217\'20\'19 upper levels. However, sellers will look to drive ETH below $2,500. If this level is breached, ETH could slide as low as $2,200.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (SOL) recovery has hit a roadblock in the form of the 200-day SMA, which is preventing it from pushing above the $150 level. \uc2 SOL\uc2  had surged above $160 on Thursday as markets made a strong recovery. However, bulls lost steam on Friday as \uc2 SOL\uc2  dropped over 4% to $156 and remained \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the weekend. By Sunday, bears pushed the price below $150 and the 50 and 200-day SMAs to $141.59. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment over the weekend, \uc2 SOL\uc2  made a positive start to the week, as buyers pushed \uc2 SOL\uc2  to $146, an increase of 3.38%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/1cE98ggv/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers made a strong attempt to push \uc2 SOL\uc2  above $150, but with sellers active at this level, they were unable to do so. With the 200-day SMA acting as a dynamic resistance level, \uc2 SOL\uc2  could register only a marginal increase on Tuesday, as buyers and sellers both failed to move the price by any significant margin. The current session sees \uc2 SOL\uc2  down by 0.83% as buyers look to drive the price below $140. However, while \uc2 SOL\uc2  faces considerable selling pressure at $150, buyers are preventing a drop below $140. If bulls gain momentum, it could drive \uc2 SOL\uc2  above $150 and test the resistance at $155 and $160. If sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sellers can drive \uc2 SOL\uc2  below $140, it could drop to $130 or lower.\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Toncoin (TON) has seen impressive gains this week as buyers eye the $7 price level in the short term and $10 in the long term. The altcoin\u8217\'20\'19s listing on Binance has acted as a catalyst to drive its price higher as it outperforms major cryptocurrencies in the market, many of which have had a mixed week so far. If we look at the numbers, TON has registered a jump of 6.40% in the past 24 hours and a 16% increase in the past week. TON had surged by over 15% on Thursday as buyers pushed the price past $6 to $6.26. Friday saw another substantial increase, which pushed the price above the 20-day SMA to $6.60. Buyers also attempted a push to $7 but were thwarted by sellers.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/wqhFX4mK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 TON climbed to $6.69 on Saturday but fell significantly on Sunday after a 7.24% drop yanked the price below the 20-day SMA to $6.20. However, TON quickly recovered, starting the week on a positive note. Sellers started the day with incredible \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum that saw TON cross $7, reaching an intra-day high of $7.04. However, TON encountered significant selling pressure at this level, and the price dropped back to settle at $6.29, an increase of 1.40%. TON remained \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, moving above the 20-day SMA and settling at $6.47. The current session sees TON up by 4.55% as buyers look to retest the resistance at $7.\par \par \uc2 TON has been incredibly \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, and if the current trend continues, it could break above $7. Following this break, could TON eye a move to $10?\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu (SHIB) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu (SHIB) announced considerable upgrades to its ecosystem, specifically upgrades to its Shibarium protocol, introducing a new burning mechanism, and improved wallet compatibility. This is besides two upgrades already executed this year, which included a new UI and a hard fork that allowed compatibility with popular self-custody wallets. While a lot is happening in the SHIB ecosystem, its price has been relatively muted this week after a drastic decline that culminated in the August 5 market rout. SHIB has stabilized since and registered an 11.26% increase on Thursday, rising to $0.0000143.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/jpLLfy1J/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB has declined since, and by the end of the weekend, it had dropped to $0.0000133. Monday saw a recovery as SHIB rose by 4.03% to $0.0000139. However, the price fell back into the red on Tuesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned. The current session sees SHIB down by 0.94% as sellers look to drive SHIB below $0.130. For buyers to gain a foothold, SHIB must push and close above the $0.0000140 price level.\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) is another cryptocurrency that has put up a strong showing during the current week after a robust recovery following the August 5 collapse. UNI has registered an increase of 4.45% in the past 24 hours and over 9% over the week as buyers look to push it above the 20-day SMA. UNI had ended the weekend on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note, dropping by 4.35% to settle below $6 at $5.91. This came after an impressive post-August 5 recovery, during which the price hit a high of $6.32.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/SyH958i3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI began the current week on a positive note, registering an increase of 5.31% on Monday to push back above $6 and settle at $6.32. The price continued to move upwards on Tuesday, rising by almost 2% to $6.35. The current session still sees buyers in control, with UNI up by 2.42% and trading at $6.50. If UNI can push above the 20-day SMA, it could test the resistance at $7. A break above $7 could open the doors for a move towards $7.50. Sellers are expected to defend these levels, and if the sentiment turns negative, UNI could drop below $6.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) has continued to struggle this week after buyers failed to push above $5 despite a strong showing last week. DOT tanked to multi-year support of $3.60 on August 5 but quickly rebounded thanks to strong demand at lower levels. This allowed it to push back above $4 and reach $4.88 by Thursday. However, buyers lost momentum as demand dried up at higher levels, allowing sellers to wrest control. As a result, DOT fell back in the red on Friday, registering a decline of 1.84% and settling at $4.79. DOT remained \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the weekend and ended Sunday by 5.46% at $4.50.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/hFqXqYoO/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current week began with a 2% increase, but DOT fell back on Tuesday, hitting an intraday low of $4.40. The current session sees DOT marginally down as buyers continue to struggle to establish a foothold. While there is demand at lower levels, DOT is unable to push past $5 and could trade between $4 and $5 unless demand dynamics change substantially.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240815ek8e0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
