\uc2  and Cardano suggest a shifting landscape in the crypto world.\par \par \uc2 Pawfury stands out among these options with its lucrative presale, low entry cost, and 10% extra bonus, it is important that investors do their own research and due diligence. Thoroughly evaluating the risks, understanding market conditions, and considering individual financial situations will help ensure well-informed investment decisions.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240807ek8600001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 DeFi\par \b \uc2 Markets blow up, so \u8216\'20\'18the best prep is to have a plan to buy fear and sell euphoria\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 Veteran trader\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ray Salmond \par \uc2 1,548 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 August 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Markets can be unpredictable, but a veteran crypto trader explains how to profit from the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNGEzODRlNWEtNjIwOC00NDA1LWIyYzEtMjJlNzk5NDVkMTk4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Markets blow up, so \u8216\'20\'18the best prep is to have a plan to buy fear and sell euphoria\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 Veteran trader}}}\par \par \uc2 Global markets blew up over the weekend, and the onslaught carried on throughout the trading day on Aug. 5 as the DOW and S&P 500 dropped by more than 1,000 points and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price fell below $49,000. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/how-the-yen-carry-trade-wiped-out-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Nikkei 225}}}\uc2  index saw its worst one-day correction since October 1987, and the sell-off in Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s benchmark stock index was the worst trading day in 57 years.\par \par \uc2 Nearly all markets closed Aug.5 in the red, and while it seems too early to conclude that the selling is over, traders are likely wondering whether or not it\u8217\'20\'19s time to start thinking like a contrarian and handpicking assets at a discount?\par \par \uc2 To discuss what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in this week\u8217\'20\'19s volatile market, Cointelegraph spoke to Huf, the founder of Pear Protocol, a decentralized exchange that allows traders to engage in trending narratives via pair trading.\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph: From your point of view, is there something traders are drastically wrong about regarding the current crash in global markets and crypto?\par \par \uc2 Huf: Market participants are overwhelmingly positioning for a Q4 rally, with upside catalysts including rate cuts, a civil transition to a new government in the US and other crypto specific tailwinds such as \uc2 FTX\uc2  creditor repayments.\par \par \uc2 In my opinion they are less aware that if we start aggressively cutting, this will lead to sustained downside pressure on the dollar and specifically USDJPY. TradFi deleveraging takes place over days and weeks, whereas in crypto it\u8217\'20\'19s usually over in one cascade. This further downside in USDJPY can lead to a second round of yen carry trade unwinds.\par \par \uc2 Elections are usually positive equity market catalysts but given the divided nature of US society, a less than peaceful transition to a new government is a risk - including prolonged protests that morph into nationwide riots. Some other countries such as Iran and Russia may take advantage of a distracted White House and increase their military operations abroad.\par \par \uc2 Lastly, the \uc2 US Government\uc2  is yet to sell a substantial portion of their seized Bitcoin assets. A large portion of those coins (outside of Silk Road) are embroiled in a legal battle with \uc2 BitFinex\uc2  and its users. If they were to win and receive the Bitcoin, coins which had previously essentially been out of circulating supply could hit the market then we could see a \uc2 Mt. Gox\uc2  part 2 style fear, offsetting the \uc2 FTX\uc2  tailwind.\par \par \uc2 CT: As a trader, is there a lesson to be learned or a better way to prepare, play or hedge against events like the last few days?\par \par \uc2 Huf: Summer liquidity is always lower than the rest of the year, so preparing for this seasonality is key. Traders should either size down (use less leverage) in these summer months to account for this difference in market structure and/or increase your cash allocation to improve your average entry price.\par \par \uc2 Whilst tempting to think one could have simply bought VIX futures - the reality is that most of the time the vix is in contango and holding/rolling to expiry has been an expensive and fruitless endeavour.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been trending down since April in crypto. One technique for such choppy and \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions is to pair trade - i.e. you build a portfolio of long assets and offset the risk with a corresponding basket of shorts. For example, a user may still want to be long Bitcoin but be worried about drawdowns like today. One {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://beta.pear.garden/education/expressing-long-term-views-with-less-risk-of-getting-liquidated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 idea}}}\uc2  would be to be long Bitcoin and short something like \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  or \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 . You benefit from the upside when markets trend as moves tend to be bitcoin led, whilst the short leg provides protection on the downside.\par \par \uc2 As always, the best form of preparation is to have a plan to buy fear and sell euphoria. What\u8217\'20\'19s made this market hard is compared to previous cycles where dogcoins marked a clear local top, the memecoin mania extended for several weeks and months giving the illusion of sustainability. When you next see a limited pool of capital constantly rotating between narratives it will be an indicator of late cycle behaviour.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/jump-trading-ether-dump-smart-move-trouble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jump Trading\u8217\'20\'19s Ether dump: Smart move or sign of trouble?}}}\par \par \uc2 CT: Is there a better way to position directionally than just looking at potential mean reversions on deeply oversold assets like BTC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Yes, one of the misconceptions about pair trading is that you give up too much upside. That\u8217\'20\'19s not necessarily true due to the use of cross margin and sensible leverage. For example, a user may anticipate a +10% move up in \uc2 SOL\uc2 . This clearly carries a lot of risk to the downside.\par \par \uc2 However, trading something like \uc2 SOL\uc2 /ETH allows a user to capture a say 5% move instead and can be done with leverage of 2x. The gains on the long \uc2 SOL\uc2  leg offset any potential loss of being short ETH into a raising market.\par \par \uc2 However, the real power of this strategy is on the downside. Say \uc2 SOL\uc2  was to move down -5%, and ETH fell -10%, then the user is still making money regardless of if the broader market went up or down.\par \par \uc2 Whilst pair trading is not market-neutral per se due to the beta and vol of the two assets, it does provide a compelling way to amplify your view using leverage, whilst shielding you from liquidation risk.\par \par \uc2 Other instruments are starting to make their way over from TradFi including 0dte options on crypto, currently being pioneered by the likes of IVX (on Berachain).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-08/19e7b615-2a4a-4f06-93ec-8282c7a0f192.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Markets blow up, so \u8216\'20\'18the best prep is to have a plan to buy fear and sell euphoria\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 Veteran trader}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /ETH pair trading example. Source: Huf\par \par \uc2 CT: Do you think the negative funding in large caps is a head fake?\par \par \uc2 Huf: Funding has some idiosyncratic elements to it depending on the asset and the venue. For example, ETH funding is historically low partly driven by Ethena labs and the issuance of its stablecoin, the mechanism for which systematically sells ETH perps and keeps a lid on funding costs. Funding has been varying across different trading platforms too based on whether their users are aggressively long or short, so it often says more about a user base and their conditioned response (like shorting the lows) than signalling where markets may go next.\par \par \uc2 The reality is a lot of people have lost a lot of money and are revenge trading, and thus dialling up the leverage and getting stopped out before higher funding can really reset and kick in.\par \par \uc2 CT: Do these margin calls and unwinds in TradFi that we saw this week take a few days to wash out compared to crypto, and does that mean that any immediate oversold bounce in crypto is a trap?\par \par \uc2 Huf: Yes, there are two types of TradFi selling to be aware of. Discretionary and algorithmic. When vol spikes like it has - a combination of momentum funds, risk parity algos, CTAs and other systematic strategies flip their signal and start selling risk assets including equity futures. Once \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  dies down, the models reset and the trend goes back to neutral. However, discretionary allocation is often a lot slower. This involves risk and asset allocation committees slowing unwinding either in an OTC fashion or processing their trades in smaller clips so as to panic sell.\par \par \uc2 CT- Many analysts have long expected the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  to cut rates and on Aug.5, Wharton\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/08/05/whartons-jeremy-siegel-says-fed-needs-to-make-an-emergency-rate-cut.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeremy Siegel said}}}\uc2  the Fed needs to make an emergency rate cut. Meanwhile, Gradually, Then Suddenly author Parker Lewis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/parkeralewis/status/1820456889479553387"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get interesting until the Fed starts cutting rates. Max pain happens after that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s your take on rate cuts, and the true short and long-term impact they could have on equities and crypto markets?\par \par \uc2 Huf: It depends on the market context. The Fed is cutting into an economy that has been relatively strong - with GDP and employment pretty robust up until this latest NFP datapoint. Rate cuts (much like rate hikes) produce a delayed response in terms of looser credit conditions and higher consumption/spending.\par \par \uc2 In the short term, thankfully the market has gotten ahead of itself expecting a very aggressive path of rate cuts. If and when this doesn\u8217\'20\'19t manifest, it can lead to some relief especially if the economic data is good. In the long term, the bigger risk to a society is always inflation and thus the lever of interest rates has shown to be an effective tool in controlling that.\par \par \uc2 Either way, prepare for more \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  into year end as expectations have unhinged from reality.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNGEzODRlNWEtNjIwOC00NDA1LWIyYzEtMjJlNzk5NDVkMTk4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240806ek860008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
